{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q3Wcn6m7xxXw6CS2hSB9pE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing: Diagnostic Analysis of Temporal Abstraction in World-Model RL\n2\t\n3\t## Title Candidates\n4\t\n5\t1. **\"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in World-Model Reinforcement Learning: A Diagnostic Analysis\"**\n6\t2. **\"The Delusional Critic Problem in Variable-Rate Imagination\"**\n7\t3. **\"Diagnosing Value Overestimation in Temporally-Abstract World Models\"**\n8\t\n9\t## Venue\n10\t\n11\t**CoRL 2026** — Deadline: 2026-05-29\n12\t\n13\t## Narrative Positioning\n14\t\n15\tThis is a **diagnostic analysis paper**, not a method paper. We do not propose a new algorithm. Instead, we provide a systematic, controlled investigation answering: *Why does temporal abstraction fail in world-model RL?*\n16\t\n17\tThe contribution is a **closed causal chain** from mechanism to failure mode, backed by a factorial experiment design that isolates each factor. Diagnostic papers are valued when they (a) address a widely-attempted but poorly-understood failure, (b) provide actionable insight for future method design, and (c) are methodologically rigorous.\n18\t\n19\t---\n20\t\n21\t## Core Claims\n22\t\n23\t### C1: Variable-rate imagination in DreamerV3 consistently degrades performance\n24\t\n25\tTemporal abstraction via variable dt—whether learned or fixed—degrades asymptotic performance relative to the dt=1 baseline across all tested configurations.\n26\t\n27\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n28\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n29\t| Baseline stability | exp_001_baseline (dt=1) | Stable convergence ~950 eval return |\n30\t| Fixed dt=2 collapse | exp_006_fixed_dt2 (dt=2, subsample ON, H=15) | Peak 485@35K → collapse to ~135@65K |\n31\t| Fixed dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 (dt=4) | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n32\t| Learned gate collapse | exp_005 (learned gate) | Peak 541@55K → 99@145K |\n33\t\n34\t**Strength**: Strong. Three independent dt>1 configurations all show degradation. No positive result exists for variable-rate imagination in our setup.\n35\t\n36\t### C2: Trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (root cause)\n37\t\n38\t**⚠️ Causal attribution pending**: Current 008c vs 008d comparison confounds dt_embedding training with RSSM training data composition (subsample ON/OFF). exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON + dt=2 imagination + H=8) will isolate the dt_embedding variable. C2 strength is provisional until 008f completes.\n39\t\n40\tThe trained dt_embedding enables precise dt prediction in imagination, but RSSM state prediction quality at dt>1 is insufficient to support this precision. The result is systematic value overestimation (delusional critic) that drives actor learning toward incorrect policies.\n41\t\n42\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n43\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n44\t| Untrained dt_emb, no collapse | exp_008c (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval plateau ~242@55K; v/e: @35K=21.8% (0.90x) → @55K=29.1% (0.72x) → @65K=32.8% (0.58x) (declining normalized v/e, ~7x slower than trained) |\n45\t| Trained dt_emb, collapse | exp_008d (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval declining 167→146→141 @25K→35K→45K; v/e: @25K=15.5% (1.78x) → @35K=41.2% (1.71x) → @45K=69.3% (2.09x) (accelerating overestimation) |\n46\t| Both trained dt_emb → accelerating v/e | exp_006 (H=15) vs exp_008d (H=8) | 006: v/e @35K=31.1% (1.29x)→@45K=53.3% (1.61x)→@55K=93.3% (2.31x); 008d: v/e @35K=41.2% (1.71x)→@45K=69.3% (2.09x) — both show accelerating normalized v/e leading to collapse |\n47\t| Baseline v/e calibration (overshoot reference) | exp_001_baseline | v/e@35K=24.1%, @45K=33.1%, @55K=40.4%. Overshoot ratio: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x (all >1.5x = pathological) |\n48\t\n49\t**Strength**: Strong. The 008c vs 008d comparison is a controlled experiment isolating dt_embedding training as the single variable. The v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) quantitatively identifies pathological regimes: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels. **Pending confirmation**: exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) will isolate whether dt_embedding conditioning or RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics is the true cause.\n50\t\n51\t### C3: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, substantively protecting performance\n52\t\n53\tWhen dt_embedding is untrained (random fixed), the value function cannot exploit precise dt information, preventing the optimistic value drift seen in trained variants. This value growth suppression substantively protects performance: exp_008a demonstrates two complete V-shaped recovery cycles over 105K steps (peak @105K=778, 85% of baseline 916), with normalized v/e consistently suppressed at 0.59-0.93x baseline. The trained dt_embedding variant (exp_006) collapses catastrophically as its v/e ratio accelerates far past baseline levels (2.3x baseline@55K).\n54\t\n55\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n56\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n57\t| Two V-shaped recoveries (105K) | exp_008a (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | 501→563→488→608→470→584→572→778; two complete recovery cycles over 105K steps. @65K=608 (-1.3% baseline), @105K=778 (-15.1% baseline, 85% of 916). No collapse. |\n58\t| Sustained v/e suppression | exp_008a | v/e: 37.6%@55K → 37.2%@65K → 53.6%@75K → 47.5%@85K → 49.7%@95K → 38.6%@105K. Normalized v/e: 0.93x→0.66x→0.75x→0.68x→0.79x→0.59x baseline. Consistently below 1.0x, no acceleration. |\n59\t| Trained dt_emb: accelerating collapse | exp_006 (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=15) | 485→477→360→collapse; v/e: 53.3%@45K (1.61x)→93.3%@55K (2.31x) → immediate collapse |\n60\t| v/e rate comparison (H=8 controlled) | exp_008c vs exp_008d | 008c (untrained): @35K=21.8% (0.90x)→@65K=32.8% (0.58x) (normalized declining); 008d (trained): @25K=15.5% (1.78x)→@35K=41.2% (1.71x) (normalized >1.5x = pathological). ~7x slower overestimation rate |\n61\t| Baseline v/e calibration | exp_001_baseline | v/e: 8.7%@25K → 24.1%@35K → 40.4%@55K → 56.3%@65K → 65.6%@105K (stable 69-72% from 135K+). 008a normalized v/e: 0.93x@55K → 0.66x@65K → 0.59x@105K (suppressed, diverging further below baseline); 008d: 1.7x@35K → 2.1x@45K (optimistic drift) |\n62\t\n63\t**Strength**: Strong (B+ confirmed with 105K long-run data). Two complete V-shaped recovery cycles (501→608→470→778) with normalized v/e consistently 0.59-0.93x baseline across 105K steps. This is structural value growth suppression, not a transient delay. Contrasts sharply with exp_006's accelerating v/e (1.6x→2.3x baseline → collapse). The mechanism is clear: untrained dt_embedding prevents the value function from exploiting precise (but wrong) dt>1 predictions, suppressing the optimistic value drift that drives the delusional critic feedback loop in trained variants.\n64\t\n65\t**Diagnostic metric: v/e overshoot ratio** = experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same training step. >1.5x = pathological warning. Trained dt_emb variants: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x. Untrained: 008a normalized v/e range 0.59-0.93x over 55K-105K (consistently below baseline = healthy, diverging further from baseline over time).\n66\t\n67\t**105K long-run confirmed**: exp_008a ran to 112K steps. Normalized v/e at 105K=0.59x baseline (lowest point), confirming value growth suppression is structural, not a transient delay. The suppression strengthens over time rather than converging to baseline levels.\n68\t\n69\t### C4: Longer dt amplifies the problem\n70\t\n71\tIncreasing dt from 2 to 4 worsens degradation, consistent with RSSM prediction error compounding over longer temporal gaps.\n72\t\n73\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n74\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n75\t| dt=2 degradation | exp_006_fixed_dt2 | Peak 485, collapse to ~135 |\n76\t| dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n77\t| Monotonic relationship | dt=1 (~950) > dt=2 (peak 485@35K) > dt=4 (peak 177@25K) | Clear monotonic decline |\n78\t\n79\t**Strength**: Moderate. Only two dt values tested (2 and 4). The monotonic trend is clear but a finer grid (dt=3, dt=6) would strengthen this claim. Sufficient for a supporting claim but not a standalone finding.\n80\t\n81\t### C5: Learning signal reduction from shorter effective horizons compounds degradation but is not the root cause\n82\t\n83\tSubsampling with dt>1 reduces the effective number of learning transitions per episode. This contributes to degradation but is neither necessary nor sufficient for collapse.\n84\t\n85\t| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n86\t|----------|-----------|------------|\n87\t| Subsample OFF, still degraded | exp_008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval ~242 vs baseline ~950 |\n88\t| Subsample OFF, no collapse | exp_008a (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | eval 778@105K (85% baseline), no collapse through 112K steps |\n89\t| Subsample ON, collapse | exp_008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval 146, value overestimation |\n90\t| Horizon effect | exp_008c (H=8) vs exp_008a (H=15) | H=15 significantly outperforms H=8, both subsample OFF |\n91\t\n92\t**Strength**: Moderate. The 008c vs 008a comparison shows horizon length matters independently. But disentangling horizon from subsample effects requires additional controls. The key point—that it's not the root cause—is well-supported by 008c's stability despite lower performance.\n93\t\n94\t---\n95\t\n96\t## Story Arc\n97\t\n98\t### 1. Introduction\n99\t- Temporal abstraction is a long-sought goal in RL (options, macro-actions, skip connections)\n100\t- World-model RL (DreamerV3) offers a natural testbed: modify imagination dt without changing environment interaction\n101\t- Puzzle: all our attempts at variable-rate imagination degrade performance. Why?\n102\t- Contribution: systematic factorial diagnosis identifying trained dt_embedding → delusional critic as the root cause\n103\t\n104\t### 2. Background & Related Work\n105\t- Temporal abstraction in model-free RL (options framework, FiGAR, action repeat)\n106\t- World-model RL (Dreamer family, IRIS, TWM)\n107\t- Variable-rate planning in world models (few prior works, mostly positive framing)\n108\t- Value overestimation / delusional policies in model-based RL\n109\t\n110\t### 3. Methodology\n111\t- DreamerV3 as base architecture\n112\t- Variable-rate imagination: dt_embedding, temporal subsampling, learned gating\n113\t- **Factorial experiment design**: 2×2×2 grid (dt_embedding trained/untrained × subsample ON/OFF × H=8/15) + baselines\n114\t- Diagnostic metrics: eval return, value/eval ratio as overestimation proxy, learning curves\n115\t\n116\t### 4. Results\n117\t- **Finding 1**: All dt>1 configurations degrade (C1)\n118\t- **Finding 2**: Controlled ablation isolates trained dt_embedding (C2) — the \"smoking gun\" comparison (008c vs 008d)\n119\t- **Finding 3**: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, sustaining near-baseline performance (C3)\n120\t- **Finding 4**: Longer dt amplifies (C4)\n121\t- **Finding 5**: Horizon/subsample effects are secondary (C5)\n122\t\n123\t### 5. Discussion\n124\t- Mechanism: why trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (RSSM fidelity gap at dt>1)\n125\t- Connection to existing theory: delusional policies (Delalleau et al.), model exploitation in MBRL\n126\t- Why this is specific to world-model RL (model-free temporal abstraction doesn't suffer the same failure mode)\n127\t\n128\t### 6. Implications for Future Work\n129\t- Don't train dt_embedding jointly with value function in current world-model architectures\n130\t- RSSM prediction quality must improve before variable-rate imagination is viable\n131\t- Value growth suppression (e.g., untrained dt_embedding) as a potential mitigation direction\n132\t- Need for diagnostic methodology in temporal abstraction research\n133\t\n134\t---\n135\t\n136\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n137\t\n138\t### R1: \"Limited to one environment / one base algorithm\"\n139\t**Pre-emption**: Our claims are mechanistic (trained dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse). The causal chain is architecture-specific by design—we diagnose *why* it fails in DreamerV3, not whether it fails everywhere. The mechanism (RSSM fidelity gap) likely generalizes to other latent-dynamics models but we scope claims conservatively.\n140\t**Mitigation**: Cheetah Run is a planned experiment in our experiment schedule, not a stretch goal. We will include at least one additional DMC environment (Cheetah Run) to demonstrate generality of the mechanism.\n141\t\n142\t### R2: \"No proposed solution — what's the actionable takeaway?\"\n143\t**Pre-emption**: Diagnostic papers serve a different purpose than method papers. Identifying root causes (trained dt_embedding) and quantitative signatures (v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x baseline = pathological) gives the community concrete guidance. We explicitly outline mitigation directions (value growth suppression, improved RSSM, decoupled dt_embedding training).\n144\t**Mitigation**: Frame implications section as a \"research agenda\" with specific, testable hypotheses.\n145\t\n146\t### R3: \"Value/eval ratio is a crude proxy for overestimation\"\n147\t**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this is a proxy, not a formal divergence measure. However, the v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) consistently identifies pathological overestimation: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline v/e before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels.\n148\t**Mitigation**: Add distributional analysis of value predictions vs. realized returns if time permits.\n149\t\n150\t### R4: \"The factorial design is incomplete — missing cells in the grid\"\n151\t**Pre-emption**: We prioritized the most informative comparisons. The 008c vs 008d pair isolates dt_embedding training with all else held constant—this is the critical controlled experiment.\n152\t**Mitigation**: Explicitly present the factorial grid, mark which cells are filled, and justify the prioritization.\n153\t\n154\t### R5: \"Novelty concern — model exploitation / value overestimation in MBRL is well-known\"\n155\t**Pre-emption**: General MBRL overestimation is known (Janner et al., 2019), but the specific mechanism through temporal abstraction's dt_embedding is novel. Prior work on temporal abstraction in world models has not identified this failure mode. Our contribution is the *specific causal link*, not the general phenomenon.\n156\t\n157\t### R6: \"All results from a single seed — how robust are the conclusions?\"\n158\t**Pre-emption**: Our claims are about *mechanisms* (causal chain from dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse), not about precise numerical thresholds. The mechanism manifests consistently across all configurations (exp_005, 006, 007, 008d) — four independent experiments all show the same value/eval ratio divergence pattern. The probability of this pattern appearing by chance across 4 experiments is negligible.\n159\t**Mitigation**: Planned multi-seed runs for final paper. The factorial design (008c vs 008d) provides cross-experiment replication of the core mechanism.\n160\t\n161\t### R7: \"The factorial design confounds dt_embedding training with training data composition\"\n162\t**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this confound between 008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb) and 008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb). Experiment 008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) is designed to resolve this: it trains with dt=2 transitions (like 008d) but without dt_embedding conditioning. If 008f collapses → the cause is RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics, not dt_embedding per se. If 008f remains stable → dt_embedding conditioning is confirmed as the root cause.\n163\t**Mitigation**: exp_008f is a blocking experiment for the final paper. Results will be available before submission.\n164\t\n165\t---\n166\t\n167\t## Experiment Coverage Assessment\n168\t\n169\t| Claim | Evidence Status | Gaps |\n170\t|-------|----------------|------|\n171\t| C1 (degradation) | ✅ Strong — 3 configurations (005, 006, 007) all negative | Could add 1 more environment |\n172\t| C2 (root cause: dt_emb) | ⚠️ Provisional — pending exp_008f to resolve dt_embedding vs training data confound | Consider adding value prediction distribution analysis |\n173\t| C3 (preventing optimistic drift) | ✅ Strong (105K confirmed) — 008a@105K=778 (85% baseline), normalized v/e=0.59x, two V-shaped recoveries | None — long-term structural suppression confirmed |\n174\t| C4 (dt amplification) | ⚠️ Moderate — only dt=2 vs dt=4 | Would benefit from dt=3, but not blocking |\n175\t| C5 (horizon/subsample) | ⚠️ Moderate — confounded with other factors | Need 008c-equivalent with H=15 + subsample ON + untrained dt_emb for clean isolation |\n176\t\n177\t### Priority Actions Before Submission\n178\t1. ~~**Check exp_008a@65K**~~ — ✅ Done: 608 (-1.3% baseline), B+ confirmed\n179\t2. **Complete factorial grid analysis** — present all 8 cells, even if some are interpolated\n180\t3. **Value prediction distribution plots** — strengthen C2 beyond ratio proxy\n181\t4. **Second environment** (stretch goal) — addresses R1\n182\t\n183\t---\n184\t\n185\t## Key Figures (Planned)\n186\t\n187\t1. **Figure 1**: Learning curves — all experiments overlaid, showing degradation pattern (hero figure)\n188\t2. **Figure 2**: Value/eval ratio over training — separating healthy vs. pathological regimes\n189\t3. **Figure 3**: Factorial grid summary — 2×2 (dt_emb × subsample) with H as secondary axis\n190\t4. **Figure 4**: Causal diagram — dt_embedding → value overestimation → actor degradation → collapse\n191\t5. **Figure 5**: dt=1 vs dt=2 vs dt=4 comparison — monotonic degradation (C4)\n192\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70775007-aa31-498c-9ce8-96f28df641df","uuid":"a5a24ca5-c6b3-4f9d-8d1e-5e63530c6ebb","timestamp":"2026-05-14T06:42:31.527Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T062606/best/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing: Diagnostic Analysis of Temporal Abstraction in World-Model RL\n\n## Title Candidates\n\n1. **\"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails in World-Model Reinforcement Learning: A Diagnostic Analysis\"**\n2. **\"The Delusional Critic Problem in Variable-Rate Imagination\"**\n3. **\"Diagnosing Value Overestimation in Temporally-Abstract World Models\"**\n\n## Venue\n\n**CoRL 2026** — Deadline: 2026-05-29\n\n## Narrative Positioning\n\nThis is a **diagnostic analysis paper**, not a method paper. We do not propose a new algorithm. Instead, we provide a systematic, controlled investigation answering: *Why does temporal abstraction fail in world-model RL?*\n\nThe contribution is a **closed causal chain** from mechanism to failure mode, backed by a factorial experiment design that isolates each factor. Diagnostic papers are valued when they (a) address a widely-attempted but poorly-understood failure, (b) provide actionable insight for future method design, and (c) are methodologically rigorous.\n\n---\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### C1: Variable-rate imagination in DreamerV3 consistently degrades performance\n\nTemporal abstraction via variable dt—whether learned or fixed—degrades asymptotic performance relative to the dt=1 baseline across all tested configurations.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Baseline stability | exp_001_baseline (dt=1) | Stable convergence ~950 eval return |\n| Fixed dt=2 collapse | exp_006_fixed_dt2 (dt=2, subsample ON, H=15) | Peak 485@35K → collapse to ~135@65K |\n| Fixed dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 (dt=4) | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n| Learned gate collapse | exp_005 (learned gate) | Peak 541@55K → 99@145K |\n\n**Strength**: Strong. Three independent dt>1 configurations all show degradation. No positive result exists for variable-rate imagination in our setup.\n\n### C2: Trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (root cause)\n\n**⚠️ Causal attribution pending**: Current 008c vs 008d comparison confounds dt_embedding training with RSSM training data composition (subsample ON/OFF). exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON + dt=2 imagination + H=8) will isolate the dt_embedding variable. C2 strength is provisional until 008f completes.\n\nThe trained dt_embedding enables precise dt prediction in imagination, but RSSM state prediction quality at dt>1 is insufficient to support this precision. The result is systematic value overestimation (delusional critic) that drives actor learning toward incorrect policies.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Untrained dt_emb, no collapse | exp_008c (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval plateau ~242@55K; v/e: @35K=21.8% (0.90x) → @55K=29.1% (0.72x) → @65K=32.8% (0.58x) (declining normalized v/e, ~7x slower than trained) |\n| Trained dt_emb, collapse | exp_008d (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval declining 167→146→141 @25K→35K→45K; v/e: @25K=15.5% (1.78x) → @35K=41.2% (1.71x) → @45K=69.3% (2.09x) (accelerating overestimation) |\n| Both trained dt_emb → accelerating v/e | exp_006 (H=15) vs exp_008d (H=8) | 006: v/e @35K=31.1% (1.29x)→@45K=53.3% (1.61x)→@55K=93.3% (2.31x); 008d: v/e @35K=41.2% (1.71x)→@45K=69.3% (2.09x) — both show accelerating normalized v/e leading to collapse |\n| Baseline v/e calibration (overshoot reference) | exp_001_baseline | v/e@35K=24.1%, @45K=33.1%, @55K=40.4%. Overshoot ratio: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x (all >1.5x = pathological) |\n\n**Strength**: Strong. The 008c vs 008d comparison is a controlled experiment isolating dt_embedding training as the single variable. The v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) quantitatively identifies pathological regimes: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels. **Pending confirmation**: exp_008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) will isolate whether dt_embedding conditioning or RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics is the true cause.\n\n### C3: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, substantively protecting performance\n\nWhen dt_embedding is untrained (random fixed), the value function cannot exploit precise dt information, preventing the optimistic value drift seen in trained variants. This value growth suppression substantively protects performance: exp_008a demonstrates two complete V-shaped recovery cycles over 105K steps (peak @105K=778, 85% of baseline 916), with normalized v/e consistently suppressed at 0.59-0.93x baseline. The trained dt_embedding variant (exp_006) collapses catastrophically as its v/e ratio accelerates far past baseline levels (2.3x baseline@55K).\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Two V-shaped recoveries (105K) | exp_008a (dt=2, subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | 501→563→488→608→470→584→572→778; two complete recovery cycles over 105K steps. @65K=608 (-1.3% baseline), @105K=778 (-15.1% baseline, 85% of 916). No collapse. |\n| Sustained v/e suppression | exp_008a | v/e: 37.6%@55K → 37.2%@65K → 53.6%@75K → 47.5%@85K → 49.7%@95K → 38.6%@105K. Normalized v/e: 0.93x→0.66x→0.75x→0.68x→0.79x→0.59x baseline. Consistently below 1.0x, no acceleration. |\n| Trained dt_emb: accelerating collapse | exp_006 (dt=2, subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=15) | 485→477→360→collapse; v/e: 53.3%@45K (1.61x)→93.3%@55K (2.31x) → immediate collapse |\n| v/e rate comparison (H=8 controlled) | exp_008c vs exp_008d | 008c (untrained): @35K=21.8% (0.90x)→@65K=32.8% (0.58x) (normalized declining); 008d (trained): @25K=15.5% (1.78x)→@35K=41.2% (1.71x) (normalized >1.5x = pathological). ~7x slower overestimation rate |\n| Baseline v/e calibration | exp_001_baseline | v/e: 8.7%@25K → 24.1%@35K → 40.4%@55K → 56.3%@65K → 65.6%@105K (stable 69-72% from 135K+). 008a normalized v/e: 0.93x@55K → 0.66x@65K → 0.59x@105K (suppressed, diverging further below baseline); 008d: 1.7x@35K → 2.1x@45K (optimistic drift) |\n\n**Strength**: Strong (B+ confirmed with 105K long-run data). Two complete V-shaped recovery cycles (501→608→470→778) with normalized v/e consistently 0.59-0.93x baseline across 105K steps. This is structural value growth suppression, not a transient delay. Contrasts sharply with exp_006's accelerating v/e (1.6x→2.3x baseline → collapse). The mechanism is clear: untrained dt_embedding prevents the value function from exploiting precise (but wrong) dt>1 predictions, suppressing the optimistic value drift that drives the delusional critic feedback loop in trained variants.\n\n**Diagnostic metric: v/e overshoot ratio** = experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same training step. >1.5x = pathological warning. Trained dt_emb variants: 008d@35K=1.7x, @45K=2.1x; 006@45K=1.6x, @55K=2.3x. Untrained: 008a normalized v/e range 0.59-0.93x over 55K-105K (consistently below baseline = healthy, diverging further from baseline over time).\n\n**105K long-run confirmed**: exp_008a ran to 112K steps. Normalized v/e at 105K=0.59x baseline (lowest point), confirming value growth suppression is structural, not a transient delay. The suppression strengthens over time rather than converging to baseline levels.\n\n### C4: Longer dt amplifies the problem\n\nIncreasing dt from 2 to 4 worsens degradation, consistent with RSSM prediction error compounding over longer temporal gaps.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| dt=2 degradation | exp_006_fixed_dt2 | Peak 485, collapse to ~135 |\n| dt=4 severe degradation | exp_007_fixed_dt4 | Peak 176.9@25K, 144.4@45K (33% of baseline@45K=443) |\n| Monotonic relationship | dt=1 (~950) > dt=2 (peak 485@35K) > dt=4 (peak 177@25K) | Clear monotonic decline |\n\n**Strength**: Moderate. Only two dt values tested (2 and 4). The monotonic trend is clear but a finer grid (dt=3, dt=6) would strengthen this claim. Sufficient for a supporting claim but not a standalone finding.\n\n### C5: Learning signal reduction from shorter effective horizons compounds degradation but is not the root cause\n\nSubsampling with dt>1 reduces the effective number of learning transitions per episode. This contributes to degradation but is neither necessary nor sufficient for collapse.\n\n| Evidence | Experiment | Key Metric |\n|----------|-----------|------------|\n| Subsample OFF, still degraded | exp_008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=8) | eval ~242 vs baseline ~950 |\n| Subsample OFF, no collapse | exp_008a (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb, H=15) | eval 778@105K (85% baseline), no collapse through 112K steps |\n| Subsample ON, collapse | exp_008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb, H=8) | eval 146, value overestimation |\n| Horizon effect | exp_008c (H=8) vs exp_008a (H=15) | H=15 significantly outperforms H=8, both subsample OFF |\n\n**Strength**: Moderate. The 008c vs 008a comparison shows horizon length matters independently. But disentangling horizon from subsample effects requires additional controls. The key point—that it's not the root cause—is well-supported by 008c's stability despite lower performance.\n\n---\n\n## Story Arc\n\n### 1. Introduction\n- Temporal abstraction is a long-sought goal in RL (options, macro-actions, skip connections)\n- World-model RL (DreamerV3) offers a natural testbed: modify imagination dt without changing environment interaction\n- Puzzle: all our attempts at variable-rate imagination degrade performance. Why?\n- Contribution: systematic factorial diagnosis identifying trained dt_embedding → delusional critic as the root cause\n\n### 2. Background & Related Work\n- Temporal abstraction in model-free RL (options framework, FiGAR, action repeat)\n- World-model RL (Dreamer family, IRIS, TWM)\n- Variable-rate planning in world models (few prior works, mostly positive framing)\n- Value overestimation / delusional policies in model-based RL\n\n### 3. Methodology\n- DreamerV3 as base architecture\n- Variable-rate imagination: dt_embedding, temporal subsampling, learned gating\n- **Factorial experiment design**: 2×2×2 grid (dt_embedding trained/untrained × subsample ON/OFF × H=8/15) + baselines\n- Diagnostic metrics: eval return, value/eval ratio as overestimation proxy, learning curves\n\n### 4. Results\n- **Finding 1**: All dt>1 configurations degrade (C1)\n- **Finding 2**: Controlled ablation isolates trained dt_embedding (C2) — the \"smoking gun\" comparison (008c vs 008d)\n- **Finding 3**: Untrained dt_embedding prevents optimistic drift, sustaining near-baseline performance (C3)\n- **Finding 4**: Longer dt amplifies (C4)\n- **Finding 5**: Horizon/subsample effects are secondary (C5)\n\n### 5. Discussion\n- Mechanism: why trained dt_embedding causes delusional critic (RSSM fidelity gap at dt>1)\n- Connection to existing theory: delusional policies (Delalleau et al.), model exploitation in MBRL\n- Why this is specific to world-model RL (model-free temporal abstraction doesn't suffer the same failure mode)\n\n### 6. Implications for Future Work\n- Don't train dt_embedding jointly with value function in current world-model architectures\n- RSSM prediction quality must improve before variable-rate imagination is viable\n- Value growth suppression (e.g., untrained dt_embedding) as a potential mitigation direction\n- Need for diagnostic methodology in temporal abstraction research\n\n---\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### R1: \"Limited to one environment / one base algorithm\"\n**Pre-emption**: Our claims are mechanistic (trained dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse). The causal chain is architecture-specific by design—we diagnose *why* it fails in DreamerV3, not whether it fails everywhere. The mechanism (RSSM fidelity gap) likely generalizes to other latent-dynamics models but we scope claims conservatively.\n**Mitigation**: Cheetah Run is a planned experiment in our experiment schedule, not a stretch goal. We will include at least one additional DMC environment (Cheetah Run) to demonstrate generality of the mechanism.\n\n### R2: \"No proposed solution — what's the actionable takeaway?\"\n**Pre-emption**: Diagnostic papers serve a different purpose than method papers. Identifying root causes (trained dt_embedding) and quantitative signatures (v/e overshoot ratio >1.5x baseline = pathological) gives the community concrete guidance. We explicitly outline mitigation directions (value growth suppression, improved RSSM, decoupled dt_embedding training).\n**Mitigation**: Frame implications section as a \"research agenda\" with specific, testable hypotheses.\n\n### R3: \"Value/eval ratio is a crude proxy for overestimation\"\n**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this is a proxy, not a formal divergence measure. However, the v/e overshoot ratio (experiment v/e / baseline v/e at same step) consistently identifies pathological overestimation: trained dt_emb variants exceed 1.5x baseline v/e before collapse, while untrained variants stay at or below baseline levels.\n**Mitigation**: Add distributional analysis of value predictions vs. realized returns if time permits.\n\n### R4: \"The factorial design is incomplete — missing cells in the grid\"\n**Pre-emption**: We prioritized the most informative comparisons. The 008c vs 008d pair isolates dt_embedding training with all else held constant—this is the critical controlled experiment.\n**Mitigation**: Explicitly present the factorial grid, mark which cells are filled, and justify the prioritization.\n\n### R5: \"Novelty concern — model exploitation / value overestimation in MBRL is well-known\"\n**Pre-emption**: General MBRL overestimation is known (Janner et al., 2019), but the specific mechanism through temporal abstraction's dt_embedding is novel. Prior work on temporal abstraction in world models has not identified this failure mode. Our contribution is the *specific causal link*, not the general phenomenon.\n\n### R6: \"All results from a single seed — how robust are the conclusions?\"\n**Pre-emption**: Our claims are about *mechanisms* (causal chain from dt_embedding → value overestimation → collapse), not about precise numerical thresholds. The mechanism manifests consistently across all configurations (exp_005, 006, 007, 008d) — four independent experiments all show the same value/eval ratio divergence pattern. The probability of this pattern appearing by chance across 4 experiments is negligible.\n**Mitigation**: Planned multi-seed runs for final paper. The factorial design (008c vs 008d) provides cross-experiment replication of the core mechanism.\n\n### R7: \"The factorial design confounds dt_embedding training with training data composition\"\n**Pre-emption**: We acknowledge this confound between 008c (subsample OFF, untrained dt_emb) and 008d (subsample ON, trained dt_emb). Experiment 008f (dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON) is designed to resolve this: it trains with dt=2 transitions (like 008d) but without dt_embedding conditioning. If 008f collapses → the cause is RSSM's learned dt=2 dynamics, not dt_embedding per se. If 008f remains stable → dt_embedding conditioning is confirmed as the root cause.\n**Mitigation**: exp_008f is a blocking experiment for the final paper. Results will be available before submission.\n\n---\n\n## Experiment Coverage Assessment\n\n| Claim | Evidence Status | Gaps |\n|-------|----------------|------|\n| C1 (degradation) | ✅ Strong — 3 configurations (005, 006, 007) all negative | Could add 1 more environment |\n| C2 (root cause: dt_emb) | ⚠️ Provisional — pending exp_008f to resolve dt_embedding vs training data confound | Consider adding value prediction distribution analysis |\n| C3 (preventing optimistic drift) | ✅ Strong (105K confirmed) — 008a@105K=778 (85% baseline), normalized v/e=0.59x, two V-shaped recoveries | None — long-term structural suppression confirmed |\n| C4 (dt amplification) | ⚠️ Moderate — only dt=2 vs dt=4 | Would benefit from dt=3, but not blocking |\n| C5 (horizon/subsample) | ⚠️ Moderate — confounded with other factors | Need 008c-equivalent with H=15 + subsample ON + untrained dt_emb for clean isolation |\n\n### Priority Actions Before Submission\n1. ~~**Check exp_008a@65K**~~ — ✅ Done: 608 (-1.3% baseline), B+ confirmed\n2. **Complete factorial grid analysis** — present all 8 cells, even if some are interpolated\n3. **Value prediction distribution plots** — strengthen C2 beyond ratio proxy\n4. **Second environment** (stretch goal) — addresses R1\n\n---\n\n## Key Figures (Planned)\n\n1. **Figure 1**: Learning curves — all experiments overlaid, showing degradation pattern (hero figure)\n2. **Figure 2**: Value/eval ratio over training — separating healthy vs. pathological regimes\n3. **Figure 3**: Factorial grid summary — 2×2 (dt_emb × subsample) with H as secondary axis\n4. **Figure 4**: Causal diagram — dt_embedding → value overestimation → actor degradation → collapse\n5. **Figure 5**: dt=1 vs dt=2 vs dt=4 comparison — monotonic degradation (C4)\n","numLines":192,"startLine":1,"totalLines":192}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0159bsshJP4i1dmfxWhRZjmN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk dt_embed_dim=0 H=8 — 55K completion\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"008f 已运行至 35K，继续至 55K+ 确认 normalized v/e 持续收敛， eval 稳定在 190-260 范围，与 008d 的 diverging pattern 形成完整对照。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"eval_return_45K\": 215,\n7\t      \"eval_return_55K\": 230,\n8\t      \"eval_return_65K\": 238,\n9\t      \"value_mean_45K\": 55.0,\n10\t      \"value_mean_55K\": 76.0,\n11\t      \"value_eval_ratio_45K\": 0.256,\n12\t      \"value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.33,\n13\t      \"normalized_ve_45K\": 0.77,\n14\t      \"normalized_ve_55K\": 0.82,\n15\t      \"normalized_ve_65K\": 0.72,\n16\t      \"vs_baseline_55K\": \"-63.2%\",\n17\t      \"collapse\": false,\n18\t      \"gate_dt_mean\": 2\n19\t    },\n20\t    \"tables\": [\n21\t      {\n22\t        \"title\": \"008f vs 008d — Causal Isolation\",\n23\t        \"rows\": [\n24\t          [\n25\t            \"Metric\",\n26\t            \"008f (no dt_emb)\",\n27\t            \"008d (trained dt_emb)\",\n28\t            \"Interpretation\"\n29\t          ],\n30\t          [\n31\t            \"normalized_ve_25K\",\n32\t            \"1.02x\",\n33\t            \"1.78x\",\n34\t            \"008d 已进入 pathological\"\n35\t          ],\n36\t          [\n37\t            \"normalized_ve_35K\",\n38\t            \"0.73x\",\n39\t            \"1.71x\",\n40\t            \"008f 收敛，008d 持续 diverge\"\n41\t          ],\n42\t          [\n43\t            \"normalized_ve_45K\",\n44\t            \"0.77x (pred)\",\n45\t            \"2.09x\",\n46\t            \"gap 扩大至 2.7x 差异\"\n47\t          ],\n48\t          [\n49\t            \"normalized_ve_55K\",\n50\t            \"0.82x (pred)\",\n51\t            \"— (已 collapse)\",\n52\t            \"008f 稳定\"\n53\t          ],\n54\t          [\n55\t            \"eval_return_45K\",\n56\t            \"~215 (pred)\",\n57\t            \"140.8\",\n58\t            \"008f 略高，无 collapse\"\n59\t          ],\n60\t          [\n61\t            \"collapse\",\n62\t            \"No\",\n63\t            \"Yes (@35K)\",\n64\t            \"单变量隔离确认\"\n65\t          ]\n66\t        ]\n67\t      }\n68\t    ],\n69\t    \"figures\": [],\n70\t    \"analysis\": \"这是整篇论文的 smoking gun。008f 与 008d 仅差一个变量：dt_embedding。 008d 有 trained dt_embedding → normalized v/e 1.78x→2.09x → collapse； 008f 无 dt_embedding → normalized v/e 0.73x→0.82x → stable。 因果归因闭合：dt_embedding conditioning 是 delusional critic 的充要条件。 RSSM 的 dt=2 prediction quality 本身不足以触发 collapse（008f 证明）， 但给 critic 提供 dt 信息后，critic 会 exploit 这些不准确的 dt-conditioned  predictions 来系统性高估 value。\\n\\n\\ndt_embed_dim=0 意味着 critic 在 imagination 中无法获得 dt 信息， 因此无法对 dt=2 步骤做出 dt-specific 的价值估计。 RSSM 仍然用 dt=2 transition 训练（subsample ON），所以 world model  对 dt=2 dynamics 的预测质量仍然有限，限制了绝对性能（~230 vs baseline 950）。 但关键是：没有 dt_embedding → critic 不会因 dt-conditioned  overestimation 而 diverge。v/e 应跟随或略低于 baseline 的自然增长曲线 （normalized ~0.7-0.85x），绝不会出现 008d 那种 >1.5x 的 pathological  overshoot。45K→55K 的 normalized v/e 从 0.77→0.82 是自然漂移， 不是 accelerating divergence。这直接证明 dt_embedding conditioning  （而非 RSSM 的 dt=2 dynamics 本身）是 delusional critic 的 root cause。\\n\"\n71\t  },\n72\t  {\n73\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk untrained dt_emb + subsample ON H=15\",\n74\t    \"description\": \"解耦 008a 的 B+ protection 来源：是 untrained dt_emb 还是 subsample OFF？ 008e_v3 已在运行（45K 数据：382.2, v/e=0.876x），预测完整轨迹。\\n\",\n75\t    \"results\": {\n76\t      \"eval_return_45K\": 382,\n77\t      \"eval_return_55K\": 430,\n78\t      \"eval_return_65K\": 490,\n79\t      \"eval_return_75K\": 460,\n80\t      \"eval_return_85K\": 520,\n81\t      \"eval_return_95K\": 550,\n82\t      \"eval_return_105K\": 640,\n83\t      \"value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.36,\n84\t      \"value_eval_ratio_65K\": 0.4,\n85\t      \"value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.45,\n86\t      \"normalized_ve_45K\": 0.88,\n87\t      \"normalized_ve_55K\": 0.89,\n88\t      \"normalized_ve_65K\": 0.71,\n89\t      \"normalized_ve_105K\": 0.69,\n90\t      \"vs_baseline_105K\": \"-30.1%\",\n91\t      \"collapse\": false\n92\t    },\n93\t    \"tables\": [\n94\t      {\n95\t        \"title\": \"B+ Protection 归因：008a vs 008e_v2 vs 008d\",\n96\t        \"rows\": [\n97\t          [\n98\t            \"Config\",\n99\t            \"subsample\",\n100\t            \"dt_emb\",\n101\t            \"eval@105K\",\n102\t            \"norm_ve@105K\",\n103\t            \"collapse\"\n104\t          ],\n105\t          [\n106\t            \"008a\",\n107\t            \"OFF\",\n108\t            \"untrained\",\n109\t            \"778\",\n110\t            \"0.59x\",\n111\t            \"No\"\n112\t          ],\n113\t          [\n114\t            \"008e_v2 (pred)\",\n115\t            \"ON\",\n116\t            \"untrained\",\n117\t            \"~640\",\n118\t            \"~0.69x\",\n119\t            \"No\"\n120\t          ],\n121\t          [\n122\t            \"008d\",\n123\t            \"ON\",\n124\t            \"trained\",\n125\t            \"— (collapse@35K)\",\n126\t            \"2.09x@45K\",\n127\t            \"Yes\"\n128\t          ]\n129\t        ]\n130\t      }\n131\t    ],\n132\t    \"figures\": [],\n133\t    \"analysis\": \"008e_v2 是 C3/C5 的关键解耦实验。如果 008a 的 protection 来自 subsample OFF （更多训练数据），那么 008e_v2（subsample ON）应该 collapse。 但 008e_v2 不 collapse 且 normalized v/e <1.0x，证明 protection  的主因是 untrained dt_emb，subsample 只影响收敛速度。 这也强化了 C5：learning signal reduction 是 secondary factor，不是 root cause。\\n\\n\\nuntrained dt_emb + subsample ON + H=15 结合了两个效应： (1) untrained dt_emb 阻止 dt-conditioned value overestimation（同 008a 机制）， (2) subsample ON 减少有效训练 transition 数量，比 008a（subsample OFF）学得慢。 因此绝对性能低于 008a（640 vs 778 @105K），但同样不会 collapse。 normalized v/e 保持 <1.0x 证明 protection 来自 untrained dt_emb（而非 subsample OFF）， 因为 subsample ON 的训练数据分布与 008d 相同，唯一差异是 dt_emb 是否 trained。 相比 008a 的两次 V-recovery，这里预期振荡幅度更小（subsample ON  → 更稳定但更慢的学习信号），呈现缓慢单调上升而非剧烈 V 形。\\n\"\n134\t  },\n135\t  {\n136\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\",\n137\t    \"description\": \"2 个额外 seed 建立 baseline v/e 校准的置信区间， 为 008d/008f 多种子 normalized v/e 计算提供 per-seed reference。\\n\",\n138\t    \"results\": {\n139\t      \"seed1_eval_return_last10_mean\": 940,\n140\t      \"seed2_eval_return_last10_mean\": 960,\n141\t      \"three_seed_mean\": 950.3,\n142\t      \"three_seed_std\": 9.5,\n143\t      \"seed1_ve_35K\": 0.23,\n144\t      \"seed2_ve_35K\": 0.25,\n145\t      \"seed1_ve_55K\": 0.39,\n146\t      \"seed2_ve_55K\": 0.42,\n147\t      \"seed1_ve_105K\": 0.64,\n148\t      \"seed2_ve_105K\": 0.68,\n149\t      \"ve_35K_mean\": 0.24,\n150\t      \"ve_35K_std\": 0.013,\n151\t      \"ve_55K_mean\": 0.405,\n152\t      \"ve_55K_std\": 0.015,\n153\t      \"ve_105K_mean\": 0.66,\n154\t      \"ve_105K_std\": 0.014,\n155\t      \"ve_stable_range\": \"68-73%\"\n156\t    },\n157\t    \"tables\": [\n158\t      {\n159\t        \"title\": \"Baseline v/e Calibration (3 seeds)\",\n160\t        \"rows\": [\n161\t          [\n162\t            \"Step\",\n163\t            \"Seed 0\",\n164\t            \"Seed 1 (pred)\",\n165\t            \"Seed 2 (pred)\",\n166\t            \"Mean±Std\"\n167\t          ],\n168\t          [\n169\t            \"35K\",\n170\t            \"0.241\",\n171\t            \"0.23\",\n172\t            \"0.25\",\n173\t            \"0.240±0.013\"\n174\t          ],\n175\t          [\n176\t            \"55K\",\n177\t            \"0.404\",\n178\t            \"0.39\",\n179\t            \"0.42\",\n180\t            \"0.405±0.015\"\n181\t          ],\n182\t          [\n183\t            \"105K\",\n184\t            \"0.656\",\n185\t            \"0.64\",\n186\t            \"0.68\",\n187\t            \"0.660±0.014\"\n188\t          ],\n189\t          [\n190\t            \"Asymptotic\",\n191\t            \"~70%\",\n192\t            \"~69%\",\n193\t            \"~72%\",\n194\t            \"~70±1.5%\"\n195\t          ]\n196\t        ]\n197\t      }\n198\t    ],\n199\t    \"figures\": [],\n200\t    \"analysis\": \"baseline 多种子的意义不在于确认 Walker Walk 能解决（这是 trivial 的）， 而在于建立 v/e ratio 的 per-step reference distribution。 单种子 normalized v/e 有 ±5-8% 的 noise，三种子均值将 noise 降到 ±3-4%， 使得 \\\"008d 的 1.7x 是 pathological\\\" 的判断从 \\\"很可能\\\" 升级为 \\\"统计显著\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWalker Walk 是 DMC 中最稳定的环境之一，DreamerV3 baseline 的 seed 间方差极小。 seed 0 的 asymptotic 950.9 ± ~10 是典型值。v/e ratio 的 seed 间方差 主要来自 eval return 的随机波动（±15-20），而 value function 的收敛轨迹 高度一致（因为 world model 在此简单环境中很快收敛）。 三种子均值 ~950、std <10 为后续所有 normalized v/e 计算提供了 robust 的 per-step reference curve，使得 \\\"1.5x = pathological\\\"  的 threshold 具有统计意义（而非单种子巧合）。\\n\"\n201\t  },\n202\t  {\n203\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\",\n204\t    \"description\": \"复现 delusional critic collapse：3/3 seeds 均应在 25K-45K  出现 normalized v/e >1.5x 并触发 eval return 持续下降。\\n\",\n205\t    \"results\": {\n206\t      \"seed1_eval_return_25K\": 155,\n207\t      \"seed1_eval_return_35K\": 138,\n208\t      \"seed1_eval_return_45K\": 125,\n209\t      \"seed2_eval_return_25K\": 172,\n210\t      \"seed2_eval_return_35K\": 152,\n211\t      \"seed2_eval_return_45K\": 133,\n212\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.62,\n213\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_45K\": 1.95,\n214\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.8,\n215\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_45K\": 2.15,\n216\t      \"three_seed_collapse_count\": 3,\n217\t      \"three_seed_peak_return_mean\": 165,\n218\t      \"three_seed_peak_return_std\": 12,\n219\t      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_mean\": 2.06,\n220\t      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_std\": 0.13\n221\t    },\n222\t    \"tables\": [\n223\t      {\n224\t        \"title\": \"008d Collapse Replication (3 seeds)\",\n225\t        \"rows\": [\n226\t          [\n227\t            \"Metric\",\n228\t            \"Seed 0\",\n229\t            \"Seed 1 (pred)\",\n230\t            \"Seed 2 (pred)\",\n231\t            \"Consistency\"\n232\t          ],\n233\t          [\n234\t            \"Peak eval return\",\n235\t            \"167@25K\",\n236\t            \"155@25K\",\n237\t            \"172@25K\",\n238\t            \"Mean 165±9\"\n239\t          ],\n240\t          [\n241\t            \"Eval @45K\",\n242\t            \"140.8\",\n243\t            \"~125\",\n244\t            \"~133\",\n245\t            \"All declining\"\n246\t          ],\n247\t          [\n248\t            \"Norm v/e @35K\",\n249\t            \"1.71x\",\n250\t            \"1.62x\",\n251\t            \"1.80x\",\n252\t            \"All >1.5x ✓\"\n253\t          ],\n254\t          [\n255\t            \"Norm v/e @45K\",\n256\t            \"2.09x\",\n257\t            \"1.95x\",\n258\t            \"2.15x\",\n259\t            \"All >1.5x ✓\"\n260\t          ],\n261\t          [\n262\t            \"Collapse?\",\n263\t            \"Yes\",\n264\t            \"Yes\",\n265\t            \"Yes\",\n266\t            \"3/3\"\n267\t          ]\n268\t        ]\n269\t      }\n270\t    ],\n271\t    \"figures\": [],\n272\t    \"analysis\": \"3/3 collapse 复现是 best tier 的 defining criterion 之一。 这将 C2 从 \\\"provisional\\\" 升级为 \\\"confirmed\\\"，因为 collapse 不是 单种子的随机异常，而是 trained dt_embedding 的必然结果。 reviewer R6 的 \\\"single seed\\\" concern 被直接消解。 seed 间一致性（normalized v/e std ~0.13）还表明 1.5x threshold  是 robust 的诊断标准，不需要 per-seed calibration。\\n\\n\\ntrained dt_embedding 导致的 delusional critic 是结构性问题，不是随机事件。 机制：trained dt_emb 让 critic 在 imagination 中为 dt=2 步骤学到 dt-specific 的 value estimate，但 RSSM 在 dt=2 transition 上的 prediction fidelity 不足以支撑这种精度 → critic 系统性高估 → actor  追逐虚假梯度 → eval return 下降 → 正反馈循环。 这个机制对初始化不敏感（dt_embedding 的训练方向由 RSSM 的 dt=2  prediction bias 决定，而该 bias 在不同 seed 中方向一致——都是 overestimate）， 因此预期 3/3 seeds 全部 collapse，seed 间 normalized v/e 的方差很小（±0.13）。 collapse 的时间点可能有 ±5K step 的偏差，但模式完全一致。\\n\"\n273\t  },\n274\t  {\n275\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\",\n276\t    \"description\": \"复现 causal control 的稳定性：3/3 seeds 的 normalized v/e  持续 <1.0x，无 collapse，与 008d 形成完美对照。\\n\",\n277\t    \"results\": {\n278\t      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 220,\n279\t      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 240,\n280\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_35K\": 0.7,\n281\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.78,\n282\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_35K\": 0.76,\n283\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.85,\n284\t      \"three_seed_eval_55K_mean\": 232,\n285\t      \"three_seed_eval_55K_std\": 16,\n286\t      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_mean\": 0.8,\n287\t      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_std\": 0.06,\n288\t      \"three_seed_stable_count\": 3,\n289\t      \"collapse\": false\n290\t    },\n291\t    \"tables\": [\n292\t      {\n293\t        \"title\": \"008f vs 008d 多种子对照\",\n294\t        \"rows\": [\n295\t          [\n296\t            \"\",\n297\t            \"008f norm_ve (3 seeds)\",\n298\t            \"008d norm_ve (3 seeds)\"\n299\t          ],\n300\t          [\n301\t            \"@35K\",\n302\t            \"0.73, 0.70, 0.76\",\n303\t            \"1.71, 1.62, 1.80\"\n304\t          ],\n305\t          [\n306\t            \"@55K\",\n307\t            \"0.82, 0.78, 0.85\",\n308\t            \"collapse, collapse, collapse\"\n309\t          ],\n310\t          [\n311\t            \"Mean±Std @35K\",\n312\t            \"0.73±0.03\",\n313\t            \"1.71±0.09\"\n314\t          ],\n315\t          [\n316\t            \"Collapse rate\",\n317\t            \"0/3\",\n318\t            \"3/3\"\n319\t          ]\n320\t        ]\n321\t      }\n322\t    ],\n323\t    \"figures\": [],\n324\t    \"analysis\": \"008f 3/3 stable + 008d 3/3 collapse = 完美的 6-point causal contrast。 effect size 极大（Cohen's d > 10），统计检验的 p-value 可以忽略。 这直接回答了论文的核心问题：为什么 temporal abstraction 失败？ 答案：因为 trained dt_embedding 让 critic exploit RSSM 的 fidelity gap。 移除 dt_embedding → 移除 exploit 通路 → 消除 collapse。\\n\\n\\ndt_embed_dim=0 从架构上消除了 dt conditioning 通路。 无论 seed 如何变化，critic 都无法获得 dt 信息，因此无法形成 dt-specific 的 overestimation。这是架构级的保护，不依赖初始化。 性能低（~230 vs baseline 950）是因为 subsample ON 减少了训练数据 且 H=8 horizon 太短，但这与 collapse 是完全不同的 failure mode。 normalized v/e 在 0.7-0.85x 范围的 seed 间方差来自 eval return  的随机波动，不会突破 1.0x，更不会到 1.5x pathological zone。\\n\"\n325\t  },\n326\t  {\n327\t    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\",\n328\t    \"description\": \"复现 value growth suppression 和 V-recovery pattern， 确认 untrained dt_emb 的保护效应跨 seed 一致。\\n\",\n329\t    \"results\": {\n330\t      \"seed1_eval_return_65K\": 580,\n331\t      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 720,\n332\t      \"seed2_eval_return_65K\": 630,\n333\t      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 810,\n334\t      \"three_seed_mean_105K\": 769,\n335\t      \"three_seed_std_105K\": 46,\n336\t      \"seed1_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.62,\n337\t      \"seed2_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.55,\n338\t      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_mean\": 0.59,\n339\t      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_std\": 0.04,\n340\t      \"v_recovery_count\": \"3/3 show at least one V-recovery\",\n341\t      \"collapse\": false\n342\t    },\n343\t    \"tables\": [\n344\t      {\n345\t        \"title\": \"008a V-Recovery Replication (3 seeds)\",\n346\t        \"rows\": [\n347\t          [\n348\t            \"Seed\",\n349\t            \"Peak@65K\",\n350\t            \"Dip (min after peak)\",\n351\t            \"@105K\",\n352\t            \"Norm v/e@105K\",\n353\t            \"V-recoveries\"\n354\t          ],\n355\t          [\n356\t            \"Seed 0\",\n357\t            \"608\",\n358\t            \"470@75K\",\n359\t            \"778\",\n360\t            \"0.59x\",\n361\t            \"2\"\n362\t          ],\n363\t          [\n364\t            \"Seed 1 (pred)\",\n365\t            \"580\",\n366\t            \"440@75K\",\n367\t            \"720\",\n368\t            \"0.62x\",\n369\t            \"1-2\"\n370\t          ],\n371\t          [\n372\t            \"Seed 2 (pred)\",\n373\t            \"630\",\n374\t            \"490@85K\",\n375\t            \"810\",\n376\t            \"0.55x\",\n377\t            \"2\"\n378\t          ],\n379\t          [\n380\t            \"Mean±Std\",\n381\t            \"606±25\",\n382\t            \"467±25\",\n383\t            \"769±46\",\n384\t            \"0.59±0.04\",\n385\t            \"All ≥1\"\n386\t          ]\n387\t        ]\n388\t      }\n389\t    ],\n390\t    \"figures\": [],\n391\t    \"analysis\": \"V-recovery 的多种子复现证明这是 untrained dt_emb 的系统性行为， 而非 seed 0 的巧合。振荡的存在表明 dt=2 imagination 仍然引入了 learning instability（vs baseline 的 smooth convergence）， 但 untrained dt_emb 将 instability 的上界限制在 \\\"振荡\\\" 而非 \\\"collapse\\\"。 这支持 C3 的核心论点：untrained dt_emb substantively protects performance。\\n\\n\\nuntrained dt_emb 的 protection 机制是架构性的（random fixed embedding  阻断 dt-specific value learning），因此 V-recovery pattern 应跨 seed 复现。 但 V-recovery 的具体时间和幅度受 exploration noise 影响较大： actor 在 random dt_embedding 下的梯度信号较弱且含噪，导致 policy  在局部最优间振荡（V 的下降段），然后通过 value function 的 slow  catch-up 恢复（V 的上升段）。seed 0 有两次 V-recovery， 其他 seed 可能只有一次或三次，但模式一致：振荡但不 collapse。 三种子均值 769±46 @105K 对应 baseline 的 84%（best tier 定义 700-850）， normalized v/e 均值 0.59±0.04 远低于 pathological threshold。\\n\"\n392\t  },\n393\t  {\n394\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\",\n395\t    \"description\": \"建立 Cheetah Run 的 dt=1 reference，包括 asymptotic return  和 v/e calibration curve，为跨环境泛化提供 second environment anchor。\\n\",\n396\t    \"results\": {\n397\t      \"seed0_eval_return_asymptotic\": 810,\n398\t      \"seed1_eval_return_asymptotic\": 790,\n399\t      \"seed2_eval_return_asymptotic\": 830,\n400\t      \"three_seed_mean_asymptotic\": 810,\n401\t      \"three_seed_std_asymptotic\": 20,\n402\t      \"ve_35K_mean\": 0.21,\n403\t      \"ve_55K_mean\": 0.38,\n404\t      \"ve_105K_mean\": 0.6,\n405\t      \"ve_stable_range\": \"62-68%\",\n406\t      \"fps\": 7.0\n407\t    },\n408\t    \"tables\": [\n409\t      {\n410\t        \"title\": \"Cheetah Run Baseline v/e Calibration\",\n411\t        \"rows\": [\n412\t          [\n413\t            \"Step\",\n414\t            \"Mean v/e\",\n415\t            \"Std\",\n416\t            \"vs Walker baseline\"\n417\t          ],\n418\t          [\n419\t            \"35K\",\n420\t            \"0.21\",\n421\t            \"0.02\",\n422\t            \"Walker: 0.24 (similar)\"\n423\t          ],\n424\t          [\n425\t            \"55K\",\n426\t            \"0.38\",\n427\t            \"0.03\",\n428\t            \"Walker: 0.40 (similar)\"\n429\t          ],\n430\t          [\n431\t            \"105K\",\n432\t            \"0.60\",\n433\t            \"0.03\",\n434\t            \"Walker: 0.66 (slightly lower)\"\n435\t          ],\n436\t          [\n437\t            \"Asymptotic\",\n438\t            \"~65%\",\n439\t            \"~3%\",\n440\t            \"Walker: ~70%\"\n441\t          ]\n442\t        ]\n443\t      }\n444\t    ],\n445\t    \"figures\": [],\n446\t    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah Run baseline 的主要目的是为 normalized v/e 计算提供  environment-specific reference。如果两环境的 v/e calibration curve  形状一致（都是 monotonic 增长到 asymptotic），则 1.5x threshold  可以 environment-agnostically 使用，大幅增强诊断工具的通用性。\\n\\n\\nCheetah Run 在 DreamerV3 中的典型 asymptotic return 为 780-850。 相比 Walker Walk（~950），Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更复杂 （连续前进、速度控制），但 RSSM 仍能有效建模 dt=1 transition。 v/e ratio 的增长曲线与 Walker Walk 类似但 asymptotic 略低（~65% vs ~70%）， 因为 Cheetah Run 的 reward scale 和 episode structure 不同， value function 的 calibration 稍有差异。 三种子方差 std ~20 略高于 Walker Walk（std ~10），因为 Cheetah Run  的探索空间更大，不同 seed 可能发现略不同的 gait pattern。\\n\"\n447\t  },\n448\t  {\n449\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n450\t    \"description\": \"跨环境复现 delusional critic collapse：trained dt_embedding  在 Cheetah Run 中触发同样的 v/e overshoot → collapse 机制。\\n\",\n451\t    \"results\": {\n452\t      \"seed0_eval_peak\": 420,\n453\t      \"seed0_eval_peak_step\": \"35K\",\n454\t      \"seed0_eval_55K\": 280,\n455\t      \"seed1_eval_peak\": 390,\n456\t      \"seed2_eval_peak\": 440,\n457\t      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_35K_mean\": 1.85,\n458\t      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_mean\": 2.2,\n459\t      \"peak_normalized_ve_max\": 2.4,\n460\t      \"collapse_count\": \"3/3\",\n461\t      \"vs_baseline_best_pct\": 52\n462\t    },\n463\t    \"tables\": [\n464\t      {\n465\t        \"title\": \"Cross-Environment Collapse Comparison\",\n466\t        \"rows\": [\n467\t          [\n468\t            \"Environment\",\n469\t            \"Config\",\n470\t            \"Peak Return (% baseline)\",\n471\t            \"Norm v/e at collapse\",\n472\t            \"Seeds collapsed\"\n473\t          ],\n474\t          [\n475\t            \"Walker Walk\",\n476\t            \"008d\",\n477\t            \"167 (18%)\",\n478\t            \"2.09x@45K\",\n479\t            \"3/3\"\n480\t          ],\n481\t          [\n482\t            \"Cheetah Run (pred)\",\n483\t            \"trained dt_emb\",\n484\t            \"~420 (52%)\",\n485\t            \"~2.20x@45K\",\n486\t            \"3/3\"\n487\t          ],\n488\t          [\n489\t            \"Mechanism\",\n490\t            \"\",\n491\t            \"Same: trained dt_emb → v/e divergence → collapse\",\n492\t            \"\",\n493\t            \"\"\n494\t          ]\n495\t        ]\n496\t      }\n497\t    ],\n498\t    \"figures\": [],\n499\t    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah Run 的 collapse 复现是论文 generalization claim 的支柱。 同一机制（trained dt_emb → v/e >1.5x → collapse）在两个 dynamics 完全不同的环境中出现，排除了 \\\"这只是 Walker Walk 的 artifact\\\"  的质疑。normalized v/e 的 pathological threshold（1.5x）在两环境中 都成立，确认了它作为 environment-agnostic 诊断工具的价值。\\n\\n\\ntrained dt_embedding → delusional critic 的机制与环境无关， 只取决于 RSSM 在 dt=2 transition 上的 fidelity gap。 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 比 Walker Walk 复杂（更高维的速度控制）， RSSM 的 dt=2 prediction error 可能更大 → collapse 可能更快更剧烈。 peak normalized v/e 在 1.5-2.5x（best tier 定义）， 因为 dt_embedding 让 critic 学到了 Cheetah Run 中 dt=2 specific  的 value pattern，但 RSSM 对这些 pattern 的预测同样不准确。 collapse 的时间可能略有提前（Cheetah Run 的更大 prediction error  → 更快的 positive feedback），peak return 约为 baseline 的 50-55% （vs Walker 中 008d 的 ~18%，因为 collapse 发生得更快， 在 agent 还没充分学习时就开始）。\\n\"\n500\t  },\n501\t  {\n502\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n503\t    \"description\": \"跨环境复现 causal control：移除 dt_embedding 消除 Cheetah Run  中的 delusional critic，normalized v/e <1.0x。\\n\",\n504\t    \"results\": {\n505\t      \"seed0_eval_55K\": 210,\n506\t      \"seed1_eval_55K\": 195,\n507\t      \"seed2_eval_55K\": 225,\n508\t      \"three_seed_eval_55K_mean\": 210,\n509\t      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_35K_mean\": 0.75,\n510\t      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_mean\": 0.82,\n511\t      \"collapse\": false,\n512\t      \"vs_baseline_55K_pct\": 26\n513\t    },\n514\t    \"tables\": [\n515\t      {\n516\t        \"title\": \"Cheetah Run: dt_emb=0 vs trained dt_emb\",\n517\t        \"rows\": [\n518\t          [\n519\t            \"Metric\",\n520\t            \"dt_embed_dim=0 (pred)\",\n521\t            \"trained dt_emb (pred)\"\n522\t          ],\n523\t          [\n524\t            \"Eval @55K mean\",\n525\t            \"~210\",\n526\t            \"~280 (declining)\"\n527\t          ],\n528\t          [\n529\t            \"Norm v/e @35K mean\",\n530\t            \"0.75x\",\n531\t            \"1.85x\"\n532\t          ],\n533\t          [\n534\t            \"Norm v/e @55K mean\",\n535\t            \"0.82x\",\n536\t            \"collapse\"\n537\t          ],\n538\t          [\n539\t            \"Collapse?\",\n540\t            \"0/3\",\n541\t            \"3/3\"\n542\t          ]\n543\t        ]\n544\t      }\n545\t    ],\n546\t    \"figures\": [],\n547\t    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah Run 的 causal control 完成了双环境 × 多种子的验证矩阵： Walker: 008f stable 3/3, 008d collapse 3/3。 Cheetah: no-dt-emb stable 3/3, trained-dt-emb collapse 3/3。 4 个 condition × 3 seeds = 12 个数据点，全部与因果假设一致。\\n\\n\\n与 Walker Walk 的 008f 完全平行的逻辑：dt_embed_dim=0 移除了 critic 的 dt conditioning 通路，阻止了 dt-specific overestimation。 Cheetah Run 中绝对性能更低（~210 vs Walker 的 ~230）， 因为 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更复杂，subsample ON + H=8 的 learning signal 更加不足。但关键指标 normalized v/e <1.0x  与 Walker Walk 一致，证明 protection 来自架构（无 dt_emb）， 不来自环境特性。best tier 定义 cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve  在 [0.5, 0.95]，预测 0.82 在此范围内。\\n\"\n548\t  },\n549\t  {\n550\t    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\",\n551\t    \"description\": \"跨环境复现 C3：untrained dt_emb 在 Cheetah Run 中同样实现 value growth suppression 和 near-baseline recovery。\\n\",\n552\t    \"results\": {\n553\t      \"seed0_eval_105K\": 620,\n554\t      \"seed1_eval_105K\": 580,\n555\t      \"seed2_eval_105K\": 660,\n556\t      \"three_seed_mean_105K\": 620,\n557\t      \"three_seed_vs_baseline_pct\": 77,\n558\t      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_mean\": 0.62,\n559\t      \"v_recovery_observed\": \"2/3 seeds show V-recovery pattern\",\n560\t      \"collapse\": false\n561\t    },\n562\t    \"tables\": [\n563\t      {\n564\t        \"title\": \"Cross-Environment C3 Comparison\",\n565\t        \"rows\": [\n566\t          [\n567\t            \"Environment\",\n568\t            \"Config\",\n569\t            \"Eval@105K (%baseline)\",\n570\t            \"Norm v/e@105K\",\n571\t            \"V-recovery\"\n572\t          ],\n573\t          [\n574\t            \"Walker Walk\",\n575\t            \"008a (3 seeds)\",\n576\t            \"769±46 (84%)\",\n577\t            \"0.59±0.04x\",\n578\t            \"3/3\"\n579\t          ],\n580\t          [\n581\t            \"Cheetah Run (pred)\",\n582\t            \"untrained dt_emb\",\n583\t            \"620±40 (77%)\",\n584\t            \"0.62±0.05x\",\n585\t            \"2-3/3\"\n586\t          ]\n587\t        ]\n588\t      }\n589\t    ],\n590\t    \"figures\": [],\n591\t    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah Run 中 77% baseline 略低于 Walker Walk 的 84%， 符合预期（Cheetah Run dynamics 更复杂 → 更大的 dt=2 prediction error  → 即使没有 dt_emb exploitation，RSSM fidelity gap 仍然限制了 absolute performance）。但 \\\"不 collapse\\\" 和 \\\"v/e <1.0x\\\" 的定性结论 跨环境一致，支持 C3 的 generalizability。\\n\\n\\nuntrained dt_emb 在 Cheetah Run 中的 protection 机制相同： random fixed embedding 阻断 dt-conditioned value learning。 subsample OFF + H=15 提供足够的 learning signal， 因此 agent 能恢复到 baseline 的 70-90%（best tier 定义 [70, 90]， 预测 77%）。V-recovery pattern 可能在 2/3 seeds 中可见 （Cheetah Run 的更大探索空间可能导致部分 seed 的振荡更不规则）， 但所有 3 seeds 都不 collapse。normalized v/e 一致 <1.0x。\\n\"\n592\t  },\n593\t  {\n594\t    \"name\": \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\",\n595\t    \"description\": \"直接量化 RSSM 在 dt=1 vs dt=2 transition 上的 fidelity gap， 为因果链提供 mechanistic foundation。\\n\",\n596\t    \"results\": {\n597\t      \"dt1_obs_reconstruction_loss\": 0.42,\n598\t      \"dt2_obs_reconstruction_loss\": 1.15,\n599\t      \"dt1_reward_prediction_loss\": 0.08,\n600\t      \"dt2_reward_prediction_loss\": 0.31,\n601\t      \"fidelity_ratio_obs\": 2.74,\n602\t      \"fidelity_ratio_reward\": 3.88\n603\t    },\n604\t    \"tables\": [\n605\t      {\n606\t        \"title\": \"RSSM Fidelity Gap\",\n607\t        \"rows\": [\n608\t          [\n609\t            \"Metric\",\n610\t            \"dt=1\",\n611\t            \"dt=2\",\n612\t            \"Ratio (dt=2/dt=1)\"\n613\t          ],\n614\t          [\n615\t            \"Obs reconstruction loss\",\n616\t            \"0.42\",\n617\t            \"1.15\",\n618\t            \"2.74x\"\n619\t          ],\n620\t          [\n621\t            \"Reward prediction loss\",\n622\t            \"0.08\",\n623\t            \"0.31\",\n624\t            \"3.88x\"\n625\t          ],\n626\t          [\n627\t            \"State prediction MSE\",\n628\t            \"0.015\",\n629\t            \"0.048\",\n630\t            \"3.20x\"\n631\t          ]\n632\t        ]\n633\t      }\n634\t    ],\n635\t    \"figures\": [],\n636\t    \"analysis\": \"这个分析将因果链从 \\\"statistical correlation\\\"（v/e overshoot → collapse） 延伸到 \\\"mechanistic explanation\\\"（RSSM prediction error at dt=2  → critic exploitation → overestimation）。fidelity ratio 的大小 也解释了为什么 dt=4 比 dt=2 更糟糕（C4）：prediction error  随 dt 非线性增长。\\n\\n\\nRSSM 是为 dt=1 sequential prediction 设计的（z_t → z_{t+1}）， dt=2 要求跳过一个中间状态直接预测 z_{t+2}。 即使通过 subsample ON 训练了 dt=2 transition，RSSM 的 recurrent  structure（GRU-based）在跳过时间步时天然会损失信息—— 中间状态的 dynamics 被 \\\"折叠\\\" 进一次 transition，增加了预测不确定性。 observation reconstruction loss 的 fidelity ratio ~2.7x  反映了这种信息损失；reward prediction 的 ratio 更高（~3.9x） 因为 reward 对 state 的微小偏差更敏感（Walker Walk 的 reward  是 smooth function of joint angles，dt=2 的 angle prediction error  直接放大到 reward error）。 这个 fidelity gap 是整个因果链的物理基础： 如果 RSSM 能完美预测 dt=2，trained dt_embedding 就不会导致  delusional critic，因为 value estimate 会基于准确的 world model。\\n\"\n637\t  },\n638\t  {\n639\t    \"name\": \"Actor entropy analysis\",\n640\t    \"description\": \"分析 collapsed vs healthy config 的 actor entropy 轨迹， 检验 \\\"delusional critic → actor confusion\\\" 的因果路径。\\n\",\n641\t    \"results\": {\n642\t      \"baseline_entropy_trend\": \"monotonic decrease 2.5→1.2 over 100K\",\n643\t      \"exp_008a_entropy_trend\": \"oscillating 2.3→1.8 with V-recovery dips\",\n644\t      \"exp_008d_entropy_25K\": 2.1,\n645\t      \"exp_008d_entropy_35K\": 2.4,\n646\t      \"exp_008d_entropy_45K\": 2.6,\n647\t      \"exp_008d_entropy_trend\": \"increasing from 25K (collapse onset)\",\n648\t      \"exp_006_entropy_45K\": 2.3,\n649\t      \"exp_006_entropy_55K\": 2.7\n650\t    },\n651\t    \"tables\": [\n652\t      {\n653\t        \"title\": \"Actor Entropy Trajectories\",\n654\t        \"rows\": [\n655\t          [\n656\t            \"Step\",\n657\t            \"Baseline\",\n658\t            \"008a (untrained)\",\n659\t            \"008d (trained)\",\n660\t            \"006 (trained)\"\n661\t          ],\n662\t          [\n663\t            \"25K\",\n664\t            \"2.2\",\n665\t            \"2.4\",\n666\t            \"2.1 (collapse start)\",\n667\t            \"2.0\"\n668\t          ],\n669\t          [\n670\t            \"35K\",\n671\t            \"2.0\",\n672\t            \"2.3\",\n673\t            \"2.4 ↑\",\n674\t            \"2.1\"\n675\t          ],\n676\t          [\n677\t            \"45K\",\n678\t            \"1.8\",\n679\t            \"2.1\",\n680\t            \"2.6 ↑↑\",\n681\t            \"2.3 ↑\"\n682\t          ],\n683\t          [\n684\t            \"55K\",\n685\t            \"1.6\",\n686\t            \"2.0\",\n687\t            \"—\",\n688\t            \"2.7 ↑↑\"\n689\t          ]\n690\t        ]\n691\t      }\n692\t    ],\n693\t    \"figures\": [],\n694\t    \"analysis\": \"actor entropy 上升是 delusional critic → policy degradation  因果路径的直接证据。这补充了 v/e ratio 的诊断（v/e 描述 \\\"critic 有问题\\\"， entropy 描述 \\\"actor 因此受害\\\"），使因果链的 \\\"最后一环\\\" 可观测。\\n\\n\\n健康的训练过程中，actor entropy 应单调下降：policy 从均匀分布 逐渐收敛到高 reward 的 deterministic action。 在 delusional critic 场景下，critic 提供的梯度方向不一致 （因为 value overestimate 的方向随 imagination trajectory 变化）， 导致 actor 无法收敛 → entropy 停止下降甚至反弹上升。 008d 在 25K（collapse onset）后 entropy 从 2.1 上升到 2.6， 表明 actor 在 delusional gradients 下变得越来越 \\\"confused\\\"。 008a（untrained dt_emb）的 entropy 振荡对应 V-recovery pattern： actor 偶尔找到好 policy（entropy 下降）但 noisy gradient  让它偏离（entropy 回升），整体呈缓慢下降趋势而非上升。\\n\"\n695\t  },\n696\t  {\n697\t    \"name\": \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\",\n698\t    \"description\": \"对比 trained vs untrained dt_emb 的 V(s) 分布 vs Monte Carlo return  分布，展示 overestimation 的 distributional 特征。\\n\",\n699\t    \"results\": {\n700\t      \"trained_dtEmb_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio\": 1.65,\n701\t      \"trained_dtEmb_V_right_tail_95th\": \"3.2x MC 95th\",\n702\t      \"untrained_dtEmb_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio\": 0.92,\n703\t      \"untrained_dtEmb_V_right_tail_95th\": \"1.1x MC 95th\",\n704\t      \"baseline_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio\": 1.05\n705\t    },\n706\t    \"tables\": [],\n707\t    \"figures\": [],\n708\t    \"analysis\": \"Distributional analysis 直接回应 reviewer R3（\\\"v/e ratio is crude\\\"）， 展示 overestimation 不是均匀的而是 state-dependent 的右偏， 这比单一 ratio 更 informative，且与 MBRL 文献中的 model exploitation  理论一致（agent 学会 exploit model error 最大的 state 区域）。\\n\\n\\ntrained dt_emb 导致 critic 系统性高估某些 state-dt combinations， 但不是均匀高估——overestimation 集中在 dt=2 imagination trajectory  经过的 state 区域。因此 V(s) 分布相比 MC return 分布呈现 右偏（right-skewed）：大部分 state 的 V 估计合理， 但一小部分 state 的 V 被严重高估（right tail 膨胀 3.2x）， 而这些 state 恰好是 actor 会在 imagination 中频繁访问的区域 → 形成正反馈。untrained dt_emb 的 V 分布几乎匹配 MC 分布 （ratio 0.92，略 underestimate——conservative is safe）， right tail 无异常膨胀。\\n\"\n709\t  },\n710\t  {\n711\t    \"name\": \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\",\n712\t    \"description\": \"追踪 trained dt_embedding 中 dt=1 vs dt=2 向量的 cosine similarity  随训练的变化，观察 differentiation 与 collapse 的时间关系。\\n\",\n713\t    \"results\": {\n714\t      \"cosine_sim_init\": 0.85,\n715\t      \"cosine_sim_15K\": 0.62,\n716\t      \"cosine_sim_25K\": 0.41,\n717\t      \"cosine_sim_35K\": 0.28,\n718\t      \"cosine_sim_collapse_onset\": \"~0.4 (25K, matching collapse onset)\",\n719\t      \"untrained_cosine_sim\": \"~0.85 (constant, random init)\"\n720\t    },\n721\t    \"tables\": [\n722\t      {\n723\t        \"title\": \"dt_embedding Differentiation Timeline\",\n724\t        \"rows\": [\n725\t          [\n726\t            \"Step\",\n727\t            \"Cosine Sim\",\n728\t            \"Norm v/e (008d)\",\n729\t            \"Event\"\n730\t          ],\n731\t          [\n732\t            \"5K\",\n733\t            \"0.85\",\n734\t            \"—\",\n735\t            \"embeddings undifferentiated\"\n736\t          ],\n737\t          [\n738\t            \"15K\",\n739\t            \"0.62\",\n740\t            \"—\",\n741\t            \"beginning to separate\"\n742\t          ],\n743\t          [\n744\t            \"25K\",\n745\t            \"0.41\",\n746\t            \"1.78x\",\n747\t            \"collapse onset — critic differentiates dt\"\n748\t          ],\n749\t          [\n750\t            \"35K\",\n751\t            \"0.28\",\n752\t            \"1.71x\",\n753\t            \"full differentiation, collapse accelerating\"\n754\t          ]\n755\t        ]\n756\t      }\n757\t    ],\n758\t    \"figures\": [],\n759\t    \"analysis\": \"cosine similarity 分析建立了 dt_embedding training dynamics  与 delusional critic onset 的 temporal coupling。 这不是相关性而是因果路径上的中间变量： training → embedding differentiation → dt-conditioned value learning  → exploitation of RSSM error → collapse。 untrained embedding 的恒定 similarity 解释了为什么 protection 是 structural。\\n\\n\\n初始化时 dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 是随机向量，cosine similarity ~0.85 （高维空间中随机向量的 typical similarity）。 训练过程中，RSSM 通过 dt_embedding 学习区分 dt=1 和 dt=2 transition， 两个向量逐渐分离（cosine sim 下降）。当 similarity 降到 ~0.4 时， critic 已经能显著区分 dt=1 和 dt=2 的 value estimate， 此时如果 dt=2 的 value estimate 基于不准确的 RSSM prediction， delusional overestimation 开始主导。这个时间点（~25K）与 008d 的 collapse onset 一致，提供了 dt_embedding differentiation → collapse  的 temporal coupling 证据。untrained embedding 的 cosine sim  恒定在 ~0.85，永远不会 trigger 这个 differentiation→exploitation 路径。\\n\"\n760\t  },\n761\t  {\n762\t    \"name\": \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\",\n763\t    \"description\": \"第三个 DMC 环境验证，强化 generalization claim。 3 configs = baseline + trained dt_emb + dt_embed_dim=0。\\n\",\n764\t    \"results\": {\n765\t      \"baseline_asymptotic_mean\": 250,\n766\t      \"baseline_asymptotic_std\": 30,\n767\t      \"trained_dtEmb_collapse\": \"3/3 seeds\",\n768\t      \"trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve\": 1.7,\n769\t      \"no_dtEmb_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.8,\n770\t      \"no_dtEmb_eval_55K_vs_baseline_pct\": 28\n771\t    },\n772\t    \"tables\": [\n773\t      {\n774\t        \"title\": \"Three-Environment Mechanism Consistency\",\n775\t        \"rows\": [\n776\t          [\n777\t            \"Environment\",\n778\t            \"Trained dt_emb collapse\",\n779\t            \"No dt_emb stable\",\n780\t            \"Norm v/e threshold holds\"\n781\t          ],\n782\t          [\n783\t            \"Walker Walk\",\n784\t            \"3/3 ✓\",\n785\t            \"3/3 ✓\",\n786\t            \"✓ (1.5x)\"\n787\t          ],\n788\t          [\n789\t            \"Cheetah Run (pred)\",\n790\t            \"3/3 ✓\",\n791\t            \"3/3 ✓\",\n792\t            \"✓ (1.5x)\"\n793\t          ],\n794\t          [\n795\t            \"Hopper Hop (pred)\",\n796\t            \"3/3 ✓\",\n797\t            \"3/3 ✓\",\n798\t            \"✓ (1.5x)\"\n799\t          ],\n800\t          [\n801\t            \"Total\",\n802\t            \"9/9\",\n803\t            \"9/9\",\n804\t            \"100% consistent\"\n805\t          ]\n806\t        ]\n807\t      }\n808\t    ],\n809\t    \"figures\": [],\n810\t    \"analysis\": \"三环境 × 多种子 = 论文最强的泛化证据。 9/9 collapse + 9/9 stable 的 binary 一致性使得 p-value < 0.001 （binomial test），即使不做 formal hypothesis testing， reviewer 也很难质疑机制的 generality。 但 Hopper Hop 是 45 GPU-hours，在 deadline 前可能无法完成。 即使没有 Hopper Hop，Walker + Cheetah 的 6/6 + 6/6 已经足够。\\n\\nHopper Hop 是 DMC 中难度较高的环境（DreamerV3 baseline ~200-300）， RSSM 对 hopping dynamics 的建模难度更大（contact dynamics,  discontinuous state transitions）。因此 dt=2 的 RSSM fidelity gap  可能更大 → trained dt_emb 的 collapse 可能更快。 但在 best tier 下，同一机制仍然 hold： trained dt_emb → v/e >1.5x → collapse；no dt_emb → v/e <1.0x → stable。 有了三个环境的一致结果，论文可以 claim \\\"the mechanism generalizes  across DMC locomotion tasks\\\"。Hopper Hop 是 P2 stretch goal， 不是 blocking，但如果完成，将使 generalization claim 从  \\\"two environments\\\" 升级为 \\\"three diverse environments\\\"。\\n\"\n811\t  }\n812\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70775007-aa31-498c-9ce8-96f28df641df","uuid":"18a84db1-42f7-4e64-8a94-da9663efa94d","timestamp":"2026-05-14T06:42:31.676Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_9/projects/event-gated-adaptive-horizon/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T062606/best/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk dt_embed_dim=0 H=8 — 55K completion\",\n    \"description\": \"008f 已运行至 35K，继续至 55K+ 确认 normalized v/e 持续收敛， eval 稳定在 190-260 范围，与 008d 的 diverging pattern 形成完整对照。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"eval_return_45K\": 215,\n      \"eval_return_55K\": 230,\n      \"eval_return_65K\": 238,\n      \"value_mean_45K\": 55.0,\n      \"value_mean_55K\": 76.0,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_45K\": 0.256,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.33,\n      \"normalized_ve_45K\": 0.77,\n      \"normalized_ve_55K\": 0.82,\n      \"normalized_ve_65K\": 0.72,\n      \"vs_baseline_55K\": \"-63.2%\",\n      \"collapse\": false,\n      \"gate_dt_mean\": 2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"008f vs 008d — Causal Isolation\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Metric\",\n            \"008f (no dt_emb)\",\n            \"008d (trained dt_emb)\",\n            \"Interpretation\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"normalized_ve_25K\",\n            \"1.02x\",\n            \"1.78x\",\n            \"008d 已进入 pathological\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"normalized_ve_35K\",\n            \"0.73x\",\n            \"1.71x\",\n            \"008f 收敛，008d 持续 diverge\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"normalized_ve_45K\",\n            \"0.77x (pred)\",\n            \"2.09x\",\n            \"gap 扩大至 2.7x 差异\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"normalized_ve_55K\",\n            \"0.82x (pred)\",\n            \"— (已 collapse)\",\n            \"008f 稳定\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"eval_return_45K\",\n            \"~215 (pred)\",\n            \"140.8\",\n            \"008f 略高，无 collapse\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"collapse\",\n            \"No\",\n            \"Yes (@35K)\",\n            \"单变量隔离确认\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这是整篇论文的 smoking gun。008f 与 008d 仅差一个变量：dt_embedding。 008d 有 trained dt_embedding → normalized v/e 1.78x→2.09x → collapse； 008f 无 dt_embedding → normalized v/e 0.73x→0.82x → stable。 因果归因闭合：dt_embedding conditioning 是 delusional critic 的充要条件。 RSSM 的 dt=2 prediction quality 本身不足以触发 collapse（008f 证明）， 但给 critic 提供 dt 信息后，critic 会 exploit 这些不准确的 dt-conditioned  predictions 来系统性高估 value。\\n\\n\\ndt_embed_dim=0 意味着 critic 在 imagination 中无法获得 dt 信息， 因此无法对 dt=2 步骤做出 dt-specific 的价值估计。 RSSM 仍然用 dt=2 transition 训练（subsample ON），所以 world model  对 dt=2 dynamics 的预测质量仍然有限，限制了绝对性能（~230 vs baseline 950）。 但关键是：没有 dt_embedding → critic 不会因 dt-conditioned  overestimation 而 diverge。v/e 应跟随或略低于 baseline 的自然增长曲线 （normalized ~0.7-0.85x），绝不会出现 008d 那种 >1.5x 的 pathological  overshoot。45K→55K 的 normalized v/e 从 0.77→0.82 是自然漂移， 不是 accelerating divergence。这直接证明 dt_embedding conditioning  （而非 RSSM 的 dt=2 dynamics 本身）是 delusional critic 的 root cause。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk untrained dt_emb + subsample ON H=15\",\n    \"description\": \"解耦 008a 的 B+ protection 来源：是 untrained dt_emb 还是 subsample OFF？ 008e_v3 已在运行（45K 数据：382.2, v/e=0.876x），预测完整轨迹。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"eval_return_45K\": 382,\n      \"eval_return_55K\": 430,\n      \"eval_return_65K\": 490,\n      \"eval_return_75K\": 460,\n      \"eval_return_85K\": 520,\n      \"eval_return_95K\": 550,\n      \"eval_return_105K\": 640,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_55K\": 0.36,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_65K\": 0.4,\n      \"value_eval_ratio_105K\": 0.45,\n      \"normalized_ve_45K\": 0.88,\n      \"normalized_ve_55K\": 0.89,\n      \"normalized_ve_65K\": 0.71,\n      \"normalized_ve_105K\": 0.69,\n      \"vs_baseline_105K\": \"-30.1%\",\n      \"collapse\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"B+ Protection 归因：008a vs 008e_v2 vs 008d\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Config\",\n            \"subsample\",\n            \"dt_emb\",\n            \"eval@105K\",\n            \"norm_ve@105K\",\n            \"collapse\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008a\",\n            \"OFF\",\n            \"untrained\",\n            \"778\",\n            \"0.59x\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008e_v2 (pred)\",\n            \"ON\",\n            \"untrained\",\n            \"~640\",\n            \"~0.69x\",\n            \"No\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"008d\",\n            \"ON\",\n            \"trained\",\n            \"— (collapse@35K)\",\n            \"2.09x@45K\",\n            \"Yes\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"008e_v2 是 C3/C5 的关键解耦实验。如果 008a 的 protection 来自 subsample OFF （更多训练数据），那么 008e_v2（subsample ON）应该 collapse。 但 008e_v2 不 collapse 且 normalized v/e <1.0x，证明 protection  的主因是 untrained dt_emb，subsample 只影响收敛速度。 这也强化了 C5：learning signal reduction 是 secondary factor，不是 root cause。\\n\\n\\nuntrained dt_emb + subsample ON + H=15 结合了两个效应： (1) untrained dt_emb 阻止 dt-conditioned value overestimation（同 008a 机制）， (2) subsample ON 减少有效训练 transition 数量，比 008a（subsample OFF）学得慢。 因此绝对性能低于 008a（640 vs 778 @105K），但同样不会 collapse。 normalized v/e 保持 <1.0x 证明 protection 来自 untrained dt_emb（而非 subsample OFF）， 因为 subsample ON 的训练数据分布与 008d 相同，唯一差异是 dt_emb 是否 trained。 相比 008a 的两次 V-recovery，这里预期振荡幅度更小（subsample ON  → 更稳定但更慢的学习信号），呈现缓慢单调上升而非剧烈 V 形。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"2 个额外 seed 建立 baseline v/e 校准的置信区间， 为 008d/008f 多种子 normalized v/e 计算提供 per-seed reference。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_last10_mean\": 940,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_last10_mean\": 960,\n      \"three_seed_mean\": 950.3,\n      \"three_seed_std\": 9.5,\n      \"seed1_ve_35K\": 0.23,\n      \"seed2_ve_35K\": 0.25,\n      \"seed1_ve_55K\": 0.39,\n      \"seed2_ve_55K\": 0.42,\n      \"seed1_ve_105K\": 0.64,\n      \"seed2_ve_105K\": 0.68,\n      \"ve_35K_mean\": 0.24,\n      \"ve_35K_std\": 0.013,\n      \"ve_55K_mean\": 0.405,\n      \"ve_55K_std\": 0.015,\n      \"ve_105K_mean\": 0.66,\n      \"ve_105K_std\": 0.014,\n      \"ve_stable_range\": \"68-73%\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Baseline v/e Calibration (3 seeds)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Step\",\n            \"Seed 0\",\n            \"Seed 1 (pred)\",\n            \"Seed 2 (pred)\",\n            \"Mean±Std\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"35K\",\n            \"0.241\",\n            \"0.23\",\n            \"0.25\",\n            \"0.240±0.013\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"55K\",\n            \"0.404\",\n            \"0.39\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"0.405±0.015\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"105K\",\n            \"0.656\",\n            \"0.64\",\n            \"0.68\",\n            \"0.660±0.014\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Asymptotic\",\n            \"~70%\",\n            \"~69%\",\n            \"~72%\",\n            \"~70±1.5%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"baseline 多种子的意义不在于确认 Walker Walk 能解决（这是 trivial 的）， 而在于建立 v/e ratio 的 per-step reference distribution。 单种子 normalized v/e 有 ±5-8% 的 noise，三种子均值将 noise 降到 ±3-4%， 使得 \\\"008d 的 1.7x 是 pathological\\\" 的判断从 \\\"很可能\\\" 升级为 \\\"统计显著\\\"。\\n\\n\\nWalker Walk 是 DMC 中最稳定的环境之一，DreamerV3 baseline 的 seed 间方差极小。 seed 0 的 asymptotic 950.9 ± ~10 是典型值。v/e ratio 的 seed 间方差 主要来自 eval return 的随机波动（±15-20），而 value function 的收敛轨迹 高度一致（因为 world model 在此简单环境中很快收敛）。 三种子均值 ~950、std <10 为后续所有 normalized v/e 计算提供了 robust 的 per-step reference curve，使得 \\\"1.5x = pathological\\\"  的 threshold 具有统计意义（而非单种子巧合）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"复现 delusional critic collapse：3/3 seeds 均应在 25K-45K  出现 normalized v/e >1.5x 并触发 eval return 持续下降。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_25K\": 155,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_35K\": 138,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_45K\": 125,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_25K\": 172,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_35K\": 152,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_45K\": 133,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.62,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_45K\": 1.95,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_35K\": 1.8,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_45K\": 2.15,\n      \"three_seed_collapse_count\": 3,\n      \"three_seed_peak_return_mean\": 165,\n      \"three_seed_peak_return_std\": 12,\n      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_mean\": 2.06,\n      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_std\": 0.13\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"008d Collapse Replication (3 seeds)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Metric\",\n            \"Seed 0\",\n            \"Seed 1 (pred)\",\n            \"Seed 2 (pred)\",\n            \"Consistency\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Peak eval return\",\n            \"167@25K\",\n            \"155@25K\",\n            \"172@25K\",\n            \"Mean 165±9\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Eval @45K\",\n            \"140.8\",\n            \"~125\",\n            \"~133\",\n            \"All declining\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Norm v/e @35K\",\n            \"1.71x\",\n            \"1.62x\",\n            \"1.80x\",\n            \"All >1.5x ✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Norm v/e @45K\",\n            \"2.09x\",\n            \"1.95x\",\n            \"2.15x\",\n            \"All >1.5x ✓\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Collapse?\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            \"3/3\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"3/3 collapse 复现是 best tier 的 defining criterion 之一。 这将 C2 从 \\\"provisional\\\" 升级为 \\\"confirmed\\\"，因为 collapse 不是 单种子的随机异常，而是 trained dt_embedding 的必然结果。 reviewer R6 的 \\\"single seed\\\" concern 被直接消解。 seed 间一致性（normalized v/e std ~0.13）还表明 1.5x threshold  是 robust 的诊断标准，不需要 per-seed calibration。\\n\\n\\ntrained dt_embedding 导致的 delusional critic 是结构性问题，不是随机事件。 机制：trained dt_emb 让 critic 在 imagination 中为 dt=2 步骤学到 dt-specific 的 value estimate，但 RSSM 在 dt=2 transition 上的 prediction fidelity 不足以支撑这种精度 → critic 系统性高估 → actor  追逐虚假梯度 → eval return 下降 → 正反馈循环。 这个机制对初始化不敏感（dt_embedding 的训练方向由 RSSM 的 dt=2  prediction bias 决定，而该 bias 在不同 seed 中方向一致——都是 overestimate）， 因此预期 3/3 seeds 全部 collapse，seed 间 normalized v/e 的方差很小（±0.13）。 collapse 的时间点可能有 ±5K step 的偏差，但模式完全一致。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"复现 causal control 的稳定性：3/3 seeds 的 normalized v/e  持续 <1.0x，无 collapse，与 008d 形成完美对照。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_55K\": 220,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_55K\": 240,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_35K\": 0.7,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.78,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_35K\": 0.76,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.85,\n      \"three_seed_eval_55K_mean\": 232,\n      \"three_seed_eval_55K_std\": 16,\n      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_mean\": 0.8,\n      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_std\": 0.06,\n      \"three_seed_stable_count\": 3,\n      \"collapse\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"008f vs 008d 多种子对照\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"\",\n            \"008f norm_ve (3 seeds)\",\n            \"008d norm_ve (3 seeds)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"@35K\",\n            \"0.73, 0.70, 0.76\",\n            \"1.71, 1.62, 1.80\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"@55K\",\n            \"0.82, 0.78, 0.85\",\n            \"collapse, collapse, collapse\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean±Std @35K\",\n            \"0.73±0.03\",\n            \"1.71±0.09\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Collapse rate\",\n            \"0/3\",\n            \"3/3\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"008f 3/3 stable + 008d 3/3 collapse = 完美的 6-point causal contrast。 effect size 极大（Cohen's d > 10），统计检验的 p-value 可以忽略。 这直接回答了论文的核心问题：为什么 temporal abstraction 失败？ 答案：因为 trained dt_embedding 让 critic exploit RSSM 的 fidelity gap。 移除 dt_embedding → 移除 exploit 通路 → 消除 collapse。\\n\\n\\ndt_embed_dim=0 从架构上消除了 dt conditioning 通路。 无论 seed 如何变化，critic 都无法获得 dt 信息，因此无法形成 dt-specific 的 overestimation。这是架构级的保护，不依赖初始化。 性能低（~230 vs baseline 950）是因为 subsample ON 减少了训练数据 且 H=8 horizon 太短，但这与 collapse 是完全不同的 failure mode。 normalized v/e 在 0.7-0.85x 范围的 seed 间方差来自 eval return  的随机波动，不会突破 1.0x，更不会到 1.5x pathological zone。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\",\n    \"description\": \"复现 value growth suppression 和 V-recovery pattern， 确认 untrained dt_emb 的保护效应跨 seed 一致。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed1_eval_return_65K\": 580,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_105K\": 720,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_65K\": 630,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_105K\": 810,\n      \"three_seed_mean_105K\": 769,\n      \"three_seed_std_105K\": 46,\n      \"seed1_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.62,\n      \"seed2_normalized_ve_105K\": 0.55,\n      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_mean\": 0.59,\n      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_std\": 0.04,\n      \"v_recovery_count\": \"3/3 show at least one V-recovery\",\n      \"collapse\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"008a V-Recovery Replication (3 seeds)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Seed\",\n            \"Peak@65K\",\n            \"Dip (min after peak)\",\n            \"@105K\",\n            \"Norm v/e@105K\",\n            \"V-recoveries\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Seed 0\",\n            \"608\",\n            \"470@75K\",\n            \"778\",\n            \"0.59x\",\n            \"2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Seed 1 (pred)\",\n            \"580\",\n            \"440@75K\",\n            \"720\",\n            \"0.62x\",\n            \"1-2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Seed 2 (pred)\",\n            \"630\",\n            \"490@85K\",\n            \"810\",\n            \"0.55x\",\n            \"2\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mean±Std\",\n            \"606±25\",\n            \"467±25\",\n            \"769±46\",\n            \"0.59±0.04\",\n            \"All ≥1\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"V-recovery 的多种子复现证明这是 untrained dt_emb 的系统性行为， 而非 seed 0 的巧合。振荡的存在表明 dt=2 imagination 仍然引入了 learning instability（vs baseline 的 smooth convergence）， 但 untrained dt_emb 将 instability 的上界限制在 \\\"振荡\\\" 而非 \\\"collapse\\\"。 这支持 C3 的核心论点：untrained dt_emb substantively protects performance。\\n\\n\\nuntrained dt_emb 的 protection 机制是架构性的（random fixed embedding  阻断 dt-specific value learning），因此 V-recovery pattern 应跨 seed 复现。 但 V-recovery 的具体时间和幅度受 exploration noise 影响较大： actor 在 random dt_embedding 下的梯度信号较弱且含噪，导致 policy  在局部最优间振荡（V 的下降段），然后通过 value function 的 slow  catch-up 恢复（V 的上升段）。seed 0 有两次 V-recovery， 其他 seed 可能只有一次或三次，但模式一致：振荡但不 collapse。 三种子均值 769±46 @105K 对应 baseline 的 84%（best tier 定义 700-850）， normalized v/e 均值 0.59±0.04 远低于 pathological threshold。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"建立 Cheetah Run 的 dt=1 reference，包括 asymptotic return  和 v/e calibration curve，为跨环境泛化提供 second environment anchor。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed0_eval_return_asymptotic\": 810,\n      \"seed1_eval_return_asymptotic\": 790,\n      \"seed2_eval_return_asymptotic\": 830,\n      \"three_seed_mean_asymptotic\": 810,\n      \"three_seed_std_asymptotic\": 20,\n      \"ve_35K_mean\": 0.21,\n      \"ve_55K_mean\": 0.38,\n      \"ve_105K_mean\": 0.6,\n      \"ve_stable_range\": \"62-68%\",\n      \"fps\": 7.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cheetah Run Baseline v/e Calibration\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Step\",\n            \"Mean v/e\",\n            \"Std\",\n            \"vs Walker baseline\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"35K\",\n            \"0.21\",\n            \"0.02\",\n            \"Walker: 0.24 (similar)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"55K\",\n            \"0.38\",\n            \"0.03\",\n            \"Walker: 0.40 (similar)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"105K\",\n            \"0.60\",\n            \"0.03\",\n            \"Walker: 0.66 (slightly lower)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Asymptotic\",\n            \"~65%\",\n            \"~3%\",\n            \"Walker: ~70%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah Run baseline 的主要目的是为 normalized v/e 计算提供  environment-specific reference。如果两环境的 v/e calibration curve  形状一致（都是 monotonic 增长到 asymptotic），则 1.5x threshold  可以 environment-agnostically 使用，大幅增强诊断工具的通用性。\\n\\n\\nCheetah Run 在 DreamerV3 中的典型 asymptotic return 为 780-850。 相比 Walker Walk（~950），Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更复杂 （连续前进、速度控制），但 RSSM 仍能有效建模 dt=1 transition。 v/e ratio 的增长曲线与 Walker Walk 类似但 asymptotic 略低（~65% vs ~70%）， 因为 Cheetah Run 的 reward scale 和 episode structure 不同， value function 的 calibration 稍有差异。 三种子方差 std ~20 略高于 Walker Walk（std ~10），因为 Cheetah Run  的探索空间更大，不同 seed 可能发现略不同的 gait pattern。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"跨环境复现 delusional critic collapse：trained dt_embedding  在 Cheetah Run 中触发同样的 v/e overshoot → collapse 机制。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed0_eval_peak\": 420,\n      \"seed0_eval_peak_step\": \"35K\",\n      \"seed0_eval_55K\": 280,\n      \"seed1_eval_peak\": 390,\n      \"seed2_eval_peak\": 440,\n      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_35K_mean\": 1.85,\n      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_45K_mean\": 2.2,\n      \"peak_normalized_ve_max\": 2.4,\n      \"collapse_count\": \"3/3\",\n      \"vs_baseline_best_pct\": 52\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cross-Environment Collapse Comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Environment\",\n            \"Config\",\n            \"Peak Return (% baseline)\",\n            \"Norm v/e at collapse\",\n            \"Seeds collapsed\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Walker Walk\",\n            \"008d\",\n            \"167 (18%)\",\n            \"2.09x@45K\",\n            \"3/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cheetah Run (pred)\",\n            \"trained dt_emb\",\n            \"~420 (52%)\",\n            \"~2.20x@45K\",\n            \"3/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Mechanism\",\n            \"\",\n            \"Same: trained dt_emb → v/e divergence → collapse\",\n            \"\",\n            \"\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah Run 的 collapse 复现是论文 generalization claim 的支柱。 同一机制（trained dt_emb → v/e >1.5x → collapse）在两个 dynamics 完全不同的环境中出现，排除了 \\\"这只是 Walker Walk 的 artifact\\\"  的质疑。normalized v/e 的 pathological threshold（1.5x）在两环境中 都成立，确认了它作为 environment-agnostic 诊断工具的价值。\\n\\n\\ntrained dt_embedding → delusional critic 的机制与环境无关， 只取决于 RSSM 在 dt=2 transition 上的 fidelity gap。 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 比 Walker Walk 复杂（更高维的速度控制）， RSSM 的 dt=2 prediction error 可能更大 → collapse 可能更快更剧烈。 peak normalized v/e 在 1.5-2.5x（best tier 定义）， 因为 dt_embedding 让 critic 学到了 Cheetah Run 中 dt=2 specific  的 value pattern，但 RSSM 对这些 pattern 的预测同样不准确。 collapse 的时间可能略有提前（Cheetah Run 的更大 prediction error  → 更快的 positive feedback），peak return 约为 baseline 的 50-55% （vs Walker 中 008d 的 ~18%，因为 collapse 发生得更快， 在 agent 还没充分学习时就开始）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"跨环境复现 causal control：移除 dt_embedding 消除 Cheetah Run  中的 delusional critic，normalized v/e <1.0x。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed0_eval_55K\": 210,\n      \"seed1_eval_55K\": 195,\n      \"seed2_eval_55K\": 225,\n      \"three_seed_eval_55K_mean\": 210,\n      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_35K_mean\": 0.75,\n      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_55K_mean\": 0.82,\n      \"collapse\": false,\n      \"vs_baseline_55K_pct\": 26\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cheetah Run: dt_emb=0 vs trained dt_emb\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Metric\",\n            \"dt_embed_dim=0 (pred)\",\n            \"trained dt_emb (pred)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Eval @55K mean\",\n            \"~210\",\n            \"~280 (declining)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Norm v/e @35K mean\",\n            \"0.75x\",\n            \"1.85x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Norm v/e @55K mean\",\n            \"0.82x\",\n            \"collapse\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Collapse?\",\n            \"0/3\",\n            \"3/3\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah Run 的 causal control 完成了双环境 × 多种子的验证矩阵： Walker: 008f stable 3/3, 008d collapse 3/3。 Cheetah: no-dt-emb stable 3/3, trained-dt-emb collapse 3/3。 4 个 condition × 3 seeds = 12 个数据点，全部与因果假设一致。\\n\\n\\n与 Walker Walk 的 008f 完全平行的逻辑：dt_embed_dim=0 移除了 critic 的 dt conditioning 通路，阻止了 dt-specific overestimation。 Cheetah Run 中绝对性能更低（~210 vs Walker 的 ~230）， 因为 Cheetah Run 的 dynamics 更复杂，subsample ON + H=8 的 learning signal 更加不足。但关键指标 normalized v/e <1.0x  与 Walker Walk 一致，证明 protection 来自架构（无 dt_emb）， 不来自环境特性。best tier 定义 cheetah_no_dtEmb_normalized_ve  在 [0.5, 0.95]，预测 0.82 在此范围内。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\",\n    \"description\": \"跨环境复现 C3：untrained dt_emb 在 Cheetah Run 中同样实现 value growth suppression 和 near-baseline recovery。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"seed0_eval_105K\": 620,\n      \"seed1_eval_105K\": 580,\n      \"seed2_eval_105K\": 660,\n      \"three_seed_mean_105K\": 620,\n      \"three_seed_vs_baseline_pct\": 77,\n      \"three_seed_normalized_ve_105K_mean\": 0.62,\n      \"v_recovery_observed\": \"2/3 seeds show V-recovery pattern\",\n      \"collapse\": false\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Cross-Environment C3 Comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Environment\",\n            \"Config\",\n            \"Eval@105K (%baseline)\",\n            \"Norm v/e@105K\",\n            \"V-recovery\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Walker Walk\",\n            \"008a (3 seeds)\",\n            \"769±46 (84%)\",\n            \"0.59±0.04x\",\n            \"3/3\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cheetah Run (pred)\",\n            \"untrained dt_emb\",\n            \"620±40 (77%)\",\n            \"0.62±0.05x\",\n            \"2-3/3\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Cheetah Run 中 77% baseline 略低于 Walker Walk 的 84%， 符合预期（Cheetah Run dynamics 更复杂 → 更大的 dt=2 prediction error  → 即使没有 dt_emb exploitation，RSSM fidelity gap 仍然限制了 absolute performance）。但 \\\"不 collapse\\\" 和 \\\"v/e <1.0x\\\" 的定性结论 跨环境一致，支持 C3 的 generalizability。\\n\\n\\nuntrained dt_emb 在 Cheetah Run 中的 protection 机制相同： random fixed embedding 阻断 dt-conditioned value learning。 subsample OFF + H=15 提供足够的 learning signal， 因此 agent 能恢复到 baseline 的 70-90%（best tier 定义 [70, 90]， 预测 77%）。V-recovery pattern 可能在 2/3 seeds 中可见 （Cheetah Run 的更大探索空间可能导致部分 seed 的振荡更不规则）， 但所有 3 seeds 都不 collapse。normalized v/e 一致 <1.0x。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\",\n    \"description\": \"直接量化 RSSM 在 dt=1 vs dt=2 transition 上的 fidelity gap， 为因果链提供 mechanistic foundation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dt1_obs_reconstruction_loss\": 0.42,\n      \"dt2_obs_reconstruction_loss\": 1.15,\n      \"dt1_reward_prediction_loss\": 0.08,\n      \"dt2_reward_prediction_loss\": 0.31,\n      \"fidelity_ratio_obs\": 2.74,\n      \"fidelity_ratio_reward\": 3.88\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"RSSM Fidelity Gap\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Metric\",\n            \"dt=1\",\n            \"dt=2\",\n            \"Ratio (dt=2/dt=1)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Obs reconstruction loss\",\n            \"0.42\",\n            \"1.15\",\n            \"2.74x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Reward prediction loss\",\n            \"0.08\",\n            \"0.31\",\n            \"3.88x\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"State prediction MSE\",\n            \"0.015\",\n            \"0.048\",\n            \"3.20x\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"这个分析将因果链从 \\\"statistical correlation\\\"（v/e overshoot → collapse） 延伸到 \\\"mechanistic explanation\\\"（RSSM prediction error at dt=2  → critic exploitation → overestimation）。fidelity ratio 的大小 也解释了为什么 dt=4 比 dt=2 更糟糕（C4）：prediction error  随 dt 非线性增长。\\n\\n\\nRSSM 是为 dt=1 sequential prediction 设计的（z_t → z_{t+1}）， dt=2 要求跳过一个中间状态直接预测 z_{t+2}。 即使通过 subsample ON 训练了 dt=2 transition，RSSM 的 recurrent  structure（GRU-based）在跳过时间步时天然会损失信息—— 中间状态的 dynamics 被 \\\"折叠\\\" 进一次 transition，增加了预测不确定性。 observation reconstruction loss 的 fidelity ratio ~2.7x  反映了这种信息损失；reward prediction 的 ratio 更高（~3.9x） 因为 reward 对 state 的微小偏差更敏感（Walker Walk 的 reward  是 smooth function of joint angles，dt=2 的 angle prediction error  直接放大到 reward error）。 这个 fidelity gap 是整个因果链的物理基础： 如果 RSSM 能完美预测 dt=2，trained dt_embedding 就不会导致  delusional critic，因为 value estimate 会基于准确的 world model。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Actor entropy analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"分析 collapsed vs healthy config 的 actor entropy 轨迹， 检验 \\\"delusional critic → actor confusion\\\" 的因果路径。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_entropy_trend\": \"monotonic decrease 2.5→1.2 over 100K\",\n      \"exp_008a_entropy_trend\": \"oscillating 2.3→1.8 with V-recovery dips\",\n      \"exp_008d_entropy_25K\": 2.1,\n      \"exp_008d_entropy_35K\": 2.4,\n      \"exp_008d_entropy_45K\": 2.6,\n      \"exp_008d_entropy_trend\": \"increasing from 25K (collapse onset)\",\n      \"exp_006_entropy_45K\": 2.3,\n      \"exp_006_entropy_55K\": 2.7\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Actor Entropy Trajectories\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Step\",\n            \"Baseline\",\n            \"008a (untrained)\",\n            \"008d (trained)\",\n            \"006 (trained)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25K\",\n            \"2.2\",\n            \"2.4\",\n            \"2.1 (collapse start)\",\n            \"2.0\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"35K\",\n            \"2.0\",\n            \"2.3\",\n            \"2.4 ↑\",\n            \"2.1\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"45K\",\n            \"1.8\",\n            \"2.1\",\n            \"2.6 ↑↑\",\n            \"2.3 ↑\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"55K\",\n            \"1.6\",\n            \"2.0\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"2.7 ↑↑\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"actor entropy 上升是 delusional critic → policy degradation  因果路径的直接证据。这补充了 v/e ratio 的诊断（v/e 描述 \\\"critic 有问题\\\"， entropy 描述 \\\"actor 因此受害\\\"），使因果链的 \\\"最后一环\\\" 可观测。\\n\\n\\n健康的训练过程中，actor entropy 应单调下降：policy 从均匀分布 逐渐收敛到高 reward 的 deterministic action。 在 delusional critic 场景下，critic 提供的梯度方向不一致 （因为 value overestimate 的方向随 imagination trajectory 变化）， 导致 actor 无法收敛 → entropy 停止下降甚至反弹上升。 008d 在 25K（collapse onset）后 entropy 从 2.1 上升到 2.6， 表明 actor 在 delusional gradients 下变得越来越 \\\"confused\\\"。 008a（untrained dt_emb）的 entropy 振荡对应 V-recovery pattern： actor 偶尔找到好 policy（entropy 下降）但 noisy gradient  让它偏离（entropy 回升），整体呈缓慢下降趋势而非上升。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\",\n    \"description\": \"对比 trained vs untrained dt_emb 的 V(s) 分布 vs Monte Carlo return  分布，展示 overestimation 的 distributional 特征。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"trained_dtEmb_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio\": 1.65,\n      \"trained_dtEmb_V_right_tail_95th\": \"3.2x MC 95th\",\n      \"untrained_dtEmb_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio\": 0.92,\n      \"untrained_dtEmb_V_right_tail_95th\": \"1.1x MC 95th\",\n      \"baseline_V_mean_vs_MC_mean_ratio\": 1.05\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Distributional analysis 直接回应 reviewer R3（\\\"v/e ratio is crude\\\"）， 展示 overestimation 不是均匀的而是 state-dependent 的右偏， 这比单一 ratio 更 informative，且与 MBRL 文献中的 model exploitation  理论一致（agent 学会 exploit model error 最大的 state 区域）。\\n\\n\\ntrained dt_emb 导致 critic 系统性高估某些 state-dt combinations， 但不是均匀高估——overestimation 集中在 dt=2 imagination trajectory  经过的 state 区域。因此 V(s) 分布相比 MC return 分布呈现 右偏（right-skewed）：大部分 state 的 V 估计合理， 但一小部分 state 的 V 被严重高估（right tail 膨胀 3.2x）， 而这些 state 恰好是 actor 会在 imagination 中频繁访问的区域 → 形成正反馈。untrained dt_emb 的 V 分布几乎匹配 MC 分布 （ratio 0.92，略 underestimate——conservative is safe）， right tail 无异常膨胀。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"追踪 trained dt_embedding 中 dt=1 vs dt=2 向量的 cosine similarity  随训练的变化，观察 differentiation 与 collapse 的时间关系。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cosine_sim_init\": 0.85,\n      \"cosine_sim_15K\": 0.62,\n      \"cosine_sim_25K\": 0.41,\n      \"cosine_sim_35K\": 0.28,\n      \"cosine_sim_collapse_onset\": \"~0.4 (25K, matching collapse onset)\",\n      \"untrained_cosine_sim\": \"~0.85 (constant, random init)\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"dt_embedding Differentiation Timeline\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Step\",\n            \"Cosine Sim\",\n            \"Norm v/e (008d)\",\n            \"Event\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"5K\",\n            \"0.85\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"embeddings undifferentiated\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"15K\",\n            \"0.62\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"beginning to separate\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"25K\",\n            \"0.41\",\n            \"1.78x\",\n            \"collapse onset — critic differentiates dt\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"35K\",\n            \"0.28\",\n            \"1.71x\",\n            \"full differentiation, collapse accelerating\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"cosine similarity 分析建立了 dt_embedding training dynamics  与 delusional critic onset 的 temporal coupling。 这不是相关性而是因果路径上的中间变量： training → embedding differentiation → dt-conditioned value learning  → exploitation of RSSM error → collapse。 untrained embedding 的恒定 similarity 解释了为什么 protection 是 structural。\\n\\n\\n初始化时 dt=1 和 dt=2 embedding 是随机向量，cosine similarity ~0.85 （高维空间中随机向量的 typical similarity）。 训练过程中，RSSM 通过 dt_embedding 学习区分 dt=1 和 dt=2 transition， 两个向量逐渐分离（cosine sim 下降）。当 similarity 降到 ~0.4 时， critic 已经能显著区分 dt=1 和 dt=2 的 value estimate， 此时如果 dt=2 的 value estimate 基于不准确的 RSSM prediction， delusional overestimation 开始主导。这个时间点（~25K）与 008d 的 collapse onset 一致，提供了 dt_embedding differentiation → collapse  的 temporal coupling 证据。untrained embedding 的 cosine sim  恒定在 ~0.85，永远不会 trigger 这个 differentiation→exploitation 路径。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\",\n    \"description\": \"第三个 DMC 环境验证，强化 generalization claim。 3 configs = baseline + trained dt_emb + dt_embed_dim=0。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"baseline_asymptotic_mean\": 250,\n      \"baseline_asymptotic_std\": 30,\n      \"trained_dtEmb_collapse\": \"3/3 seeds\",\n      \"trained_dtEmb_peak_normalized_ve\": 1.7,\n      \"no_dtEmb_normalized_ve_55K\": 0.8,\n      \"no_dtEmb_eval_55K_vs_baseline_pct\": 28\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"title\": \"Three-Environment Mechanism Consistency\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Environment\",\n            \"Trained dt_emb collapse\",\n            \"No dt_emb stable\",\n            \"Norm v/e threshold holds\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Walker Walk\",\n            \"3/3 ✓\",\n            \"3/3 ✓\",\n            \"✓ (1.5x)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Cheetah Run (pred)\",\n            \"3/3 ✓\",\n            \"3/3 ✓\",\n            \"✓ (1.5x)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Hopper Hop (pred)\",\n            \"3/3 ✓\",\n            \"3/3 ✓\",\n            \"✓ (1.5x)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Total\",\n            \"9/9\",\n            \"9/9\",\n            \"100% consistent\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"三环境 × 多种子 = 论文最强的泛化证据。 9/9 collapse + 9/9 stable 的 binary 一致性使得 p-value < 0.001 （binomial test），即使不做 formal hypothesis testing， reviewer 也很难质疑机制的 generality。 但 Hopper Hop 是 45 GPU-hours，在 deadline 前可能无法完成。 即使没有 Hopper Hop，Walker + Cheetah 的 6/6 + 6/6 已经足够。\\n\\nHopper Hop 是 DMC 中难度较高的环境（DreamerV3 baseline ~200-300）， RSSM 对 hopping dynamics 的建模难度更大（contact dynamics,  discontinuous state transitions）。因此 dt=2 的 RSSM fidelity gap  可能更大 → trained dt_emb 的 collapse 可能更快。 但在 best tier 下，同一机制仍然 hold： trained dt_emb → v/e >1.5x → collapse；no dt_emb → v/e <1.0x → stable。 有了三个环境的一致结果，论文可以 claim \\\"the mechanism generalizes  across DMC locomotion tasks\\\"。Hopper Hop 是 P2 stretch goal， 不是 blocking，但如果完成，将使 generalization claim 从  \\\"two environments\\\" 升级为 \\\"three diverse environments\\\"。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":812,"startLine":1,"totalLines":812}}}
