{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01A1YYqgWD5ahdSaGWwhxWUA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good. Now I need to write a complete LaTeX paper. Let me synthesize the experiment data and paper framing into a coherent paper.\n\nKey data points from experiments:\n\n**Experiments:**\n1. Walker Walk dt_embed_dim=0 H=8 (008f) - causal isolation, no collapse, norm v/e ~0.82\n2. Walker Walk untrained dt_emb + subsample ON H=15 (008e_v2) - B+ protection attribution, no collapse\n3. Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2 - calibration (950±9.5, v/e asymptotic ~70%)\n\n\n4. Walker Walk 008d seeds 1-2 - collapse replication (3/3, norm v/e 2.06±0.13)\n5. Walker Walk 008f seeds 1-2 - stable replication (3/3, norm v/e 0.80±0.06)\n6. Walker Walk 008a seeds 1-2 - V-recovery replication (3/3, 769±46)\n7. Cheetah Run baseline - calibration (810±20, v/e asymptotic ~65%)\n8. Cheetah Run trained dt_emb - cross-env collapse (3/3, norm v/e 2.20)\n9. Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 - cross-env stability\n\nNow I'm organizing the experimental results across both environments to show the pattern: the collapse phenomenon appears consistently when dt embeddings are trained, but disappears when they're removed or untrained, and this holds across different tasks and seeds. cross-env stable (0/3 collapse, norm v/e 0.82)\n10. Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample - cross-env C3 (77% baseline, no collapse)\n11. RSSM prediction quality dt=1 vs dt=2 - fidelity gap (obs 2.74x, reward 3.88x)\n12. Actor entropy analysis - entropy increases in collapsed configs\n13. Value prediction distribution - trained dt_emb V/MC ratio 1.65, right tail 3.2x\n14. dt_embedding cosine similarity - temporal coupling with collapse onset\n15. Hopper Hop validation - 3rd environment (9/9 collapse, 9/9 stable)\n\nCore narrative from guidance:\n- Title: \"Why Temporal Abstraction Fails\"\n- Causal chain: trained dt_embedding → RSSM fidelity gap → delusional critic → collapse\n\nI've verified this causal chain through factorial ablations across dual environments with multi-seed validation, and the v/e overshoot ratio above 1.5x emerges as a reliable diagnostic. The evidence for C2 is now confirmed, and the key takeaway for the discussion is that jointly training dt_embedding within the current RSSM architecture is problematic. Now I'm ready to write the paper.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5683,"cache_read_input_tokens":38279,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5683},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70775007-aa31-498c-9ce8-96f28df641df","uuid":"836df81f-c2b2-4a9a-9ecc-5de2ad61f339"}
